helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150402				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BEZIER_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Edit Points \</emph\>Bar appears when you select a polygon object and click \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ta	The functions provided allow you to edit the points of a curve or an object converted to a curve. The following icons are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	ta	Edit Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3159151				0	ta	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>\<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>\</link\> icon allows you to activate or deactivate the edit mode for Bézier objects. In the edit mode, individual points of the drawing object can be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ta	Edit Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	ta	Move Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierMove\"\>Activates a mode in which you can move points.\</ahelp\> The mouse pointer displays a small empty square when resting on a point. Drag that point to another location. The curve on both sides of the point follows the movement; the section of the curve between the next points changes shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	ta	Point at the curve between two points or within a closed curve and drag the mouse to shift the entire curve without distorting the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3149377\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziermove.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149377\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	ta	Move Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150115				0	ta	Insert Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3160478				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierInsert\"\>Activates the insert mode. This mode allows you to insert points.\</ahelp\> You can also move points, just as in the move mode. If, however, you click at the curve between two points and move the mouse a little while holding down the mouse button you insert a new point. The point is a smooth point, and the lines to the control points are parallel and remain so when moved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3157846				0	ta	If you wish to create a corner point you must first insert either a smooth or a symmetrical point which is then converted to a corner point by using \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3146969\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146969\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	ta	Insert Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149020				0	ta	Delete Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierDelete\"\>Use the \<emph\>Delete Points\</emph\> icon to delete one or several selected points. If you wish to select several points click the appropriate points while holding down the Shift key.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	ta	First select the points to be deleted, and then click this icon, or press Del.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147321				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3146920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierdelete.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961				0	ta	Delete Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	ta	Split Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierCutLine\"\>The\<emph\> Split Curve \</emph\>icon splits a curve. Select the point or points where you want to split the curve, then click the icon\</ahelp\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziercutline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152581				0	ta	Split Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	ta	Convert To Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148420				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierConvert\"\>Converts a curve into a straight line or converts a straight line into a curve.\</ahelp\> If you select a single point, the curve before the point will be converted. If two points are selected, the curve between both points will be converted. If you select more than two points, each time you click this icon, a different portion of the curve will be converted. If necessary, round points are converted into corner points and corner points are converted into round points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	ta	If a certain section of the curve is straight, the end points of the line have a maximum of one control point each. They cannot be modified to round points unless the straight line is converted back to a curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3149036\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierconvert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149036\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158445				0	ta	Convert To Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153199				0	ta	Corner Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148460				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEdge\"\>Converts the selected point or points into corner points.\</ahelp\> Corner points have two movable control points, which are independent from each other. A curved line, therefore, does not go straight through a corner point, but forms a corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154576				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3154201\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezieredge.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154201\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429				0	ta	Corner Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166436				0	ta	Smooth Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155510				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSmooth\"\>Converts a corner point or symmetrical point into a smooth point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel, and can only be moved simultaneously. The control points may differentiate in length, allowing you to vary the degree of curvature.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3151183\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersmooth.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151183\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	ta	Smooth Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159622				0	ta	Symmetric Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155812				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSymmetric\"\>This icon converts a corner point or a smooth point into a symmetrical point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel and have the same length. They can only be moved simultaneously and the degree of curvature is the same in both directions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3159218\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersymmetric.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159218\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866				0	ta	Symmetric Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146786				0	ta	Close Bézier				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierClose\"\>Closes a line or a curve.\</ahelp\> A line is closed by connecting the last point with the first point, indicated by an enlarged square.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3148607\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierclose.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148607\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147070				0	ta	Close Bézier				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156351				0	ta	Eliminate Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEliminatePoints\"\>Marks the current point or the selected points for deletion.\</ahelp\> This happens in the event that the point is located on a straight line. If you convert a curve or a polygon with the \<emph\>Convert to Curve \</emph\>icon into a straight line or you change a curve with the mouse so that a point lies on the straight line, it is removed. The angle from which the point reduction is to take place \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>can be set by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070300.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - Grid\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - Grid\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>is 15° by default.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3155385\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziereliminatepoints.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155385\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ta	Eliminate Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Form Navigation Bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>Toolbars; Form Navigation bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigation bar; forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sorting; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; sorting in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; sorting data\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157896				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>Form Navigation Bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ta	The \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar contains icons to edit a database table or to control the data view. The bar is displayed at the bottom of a document that contains fields that are linked to a database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	ta	You can use the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar to move within records as well as to insert and to delete records. If data is saved in a form, the changes are transferred to the database. The \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar also contains sort, filter, and search functions for data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_idN10717				0	ta	You can use the Navigation bar icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>More Controls \</link\> bar to add a Navigation bar to a form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3157910				0	ta	The Navigation bar is only visible for forms connected to a database. In the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design view\"\>Design view\</link\> of a form, the Navigation bar is not available. See also \<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	ta	You can control the view of data with the sorting and filtering functions. Original tables are not changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	ta	The current sort order or filter is saved with the current document. If a filter is set, the \<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> bar is activated. Sorting and filtering features in the document can also be configured in the \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog. (Choose \<emph\>Form Properties - Data\</emph\> - properties \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Sort\"\>\<emph\>Sort\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3149810				0	ta	If an SQL statement is the basis for a form (see \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> - tab \<emph\>Data\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data Source\"\>\<emph\>Data Source\</emph\>\</link\>), then the filter and sort functions are only available when the SQL statement refers to only one table and is not written in the native SQL mode.				20200411 15:09:53
