helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	ta	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that contains an unambiguous file specification. You can also use \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"URL notation\"\>URL notation\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3161831				0	ta	This function determines the attributes for a specified file and returns the bit pattern that can help you to identify the following file attributes:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145364				0	ta	Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349				0	ta	0 : Normal files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	ta	1 : Read-only files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	ta	8 : Returns the name of the volume				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	ta	16 : Returns the name of the directory only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3153953				0	ta	32 : File was changed since last backup (Archive bit).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020409.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	ta	If you want to know if a bit of the attribute byte is set, use the following query method:				20200411 15:09:53
