helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	ta	\<variable id=\"01030400\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01030400.xhp\"\>Organizing Libraries and Modules\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	ta	Organizing Libraries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125864				0	ta	Creating a New Library				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Libraries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ta	Select to where you want to attach the library in the \<emph\>Location\</emph\> list. If you select %PRODUCTNAME Macros & Dialogs, the library will belong to the $[officename] application and will be available for all documents. If you select a document the library will be attached to this document and only available from there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	ta	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and insert a name to create a new library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147394				0	ta	Appending a Library				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Libraries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	ta	Select to where you want to append the library in the \<emph\>Location\</emph\> list. If you select %PRODUCTNAME Macros & Dialogs, the library will belong to the $[officename] application and will be available for all documents. If you select a document the library will be appended to this document and only available from there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Append\</emph\> and select an external library to append.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	ta	Select all libraries to be appended in the \<emph\>Append Libraries\</emph\> dialog. The dialog displays all libraries that are contained in the selected file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163807				0	ta	If you want to insert the library as a reference only check the \<emph\>Insert as reference (read-only)\</emph\> box. Read-only libraries are fully functional but cannot be modified in the Basic IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	ta	Check the \<emph\>Replace existing libraries\</emph\> box if you want existing libraries of the same name to be overwritten.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to append the library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159100				0	ta	Deleting a Library				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> or click the \<emph\>Select Module\</emph\> icon in the Basic IDE to open the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Libraries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	ta	Select the library to be deleted from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150361				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152986				0	ta	Deleting a library permanently deletes all existing modules and corresponding procedures and functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ta	You cannot delete the default library named "Standard".				20200411 15:09:53
