helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03120304.xhp\" name=\"LSet Statement [Runtime]\"\>LSet Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ta	Aligns a string to the left of a string variable, or copies a variable of a user-defined type to another variable of a different user-defined type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145317				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	ta	LSet Var As String = Text or LSet Var1 = Var2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143271				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	ta	\<emph\>Var:\</emph\> Any String variable that contains the string that you want align to the left.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	ta	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> String that you want to align to the left of the string variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ta	\<emph\>Var1:\</emph\> Name of the user-defined type variable that you want to copy to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	ta	\<emph\>Var2:\</emph\> Name of the user-defined type variable that you want to copy from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	ta	If the string is shorter than the string variable, \<emph\>LSet\</emph\> left-aligns the string within the string variable. Any remaining positions in the string variable are replaced by spaces. If the string is longer than the string variable, only the leftmost characters up to the length of the string variable are copied. With the \<emph\>LSet\</emph\> statement, you can also copy a user-defined type variable to another variable of the same type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156282				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120304.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	ta	Sub ExampleRLSet				20200411 15:09:53
