helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\main0601.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148473				0	ta	Help about the Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	HasUnoInterfaces Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>HasUnoInterfaces function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149987				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03104400.xhp\" name=\"HasUnoInterfaces Function [Runtime]\"\>HasUnoInterfaces Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	ta	Tests if a Basic Uno object supports certain Uno interfaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154232				0	ta	Returns True, if \<emph\>all\</emph\> stated Uno interfaces are supported, otherwise False is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	ta	HasUnoInterfaces( oTest, Uno-Interface-Name 1 [, Uno-Interface-Name 2, ...])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ta	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	ta	Bool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159157				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ta	\<emph\>oTest:\</emph\> the Basic Uno object that you want to test.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	ta	\<emph\>Uno-Interface-Name:\</emph\> list of Uno interface names.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	ta	bHas = HasUnoInterfaces( oTest, "com.sun.star.beans.XIntrospection" )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	FileCopy Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154840				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>FileCopy statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154840				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020406.xhp\" name=\"FileCopy Statement [Runtime]\"\>FileCopy Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3149497				0	ta	Copies a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147443				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ta	FileCopy TextFrom As String, TextTo As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	ta	\<emph\>TextFrom:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies the name of the file that you want to copy. The expression can contain optional path and drive information. If you want, you can enter a path in \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"URL notation\"\>URL notation\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ta	\<emph\>TextTo:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies where you want to copy the source file to. The expression can contain the destination drive, the path, and file name, or the path in URL notation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	ta	You can only use the FileCopy statement to copy files that are not opened.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ta	Sub ExampleFilecopy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	ta	Filecopy "c:\\autoexec.bat", "c:\\Temp\\Autoexec.sav"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020406.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	ta	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	GetProcessServiceManager Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153255				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>GetProcessServiceManager function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ProcessServiceManager\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153255				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03131700.xhp\" name=\"GetProcessServiceManager Function [Runtime]\"\>GetProcessServiceManager Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	ta	Returns the ProcessServiceManager (central Uno ServiceManager).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	ta	This function is required when you want to instantiate a service using CreateInstanceWithArguments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ta	oServiceManager = GetProcessServiceManager()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149516				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ta	oServiceManager = GetProcessServiceManager()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	ta	oIntrospection = oServiceManager.createInstance("com.sun.star.beans.Introspection");				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	ta	this is the same as the following statement:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ta	oIntrospection = CreateUnoService("com.sun.star.beans.Introspection")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Libraries, Modules and Dialogs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147317				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01020500.xhp\" name=\"Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\"\>Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	ta	The following describes the basic use of libraries, modules and dialogs in $[officename] Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	ta	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	ta	Libraries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	ta	Libraries serve as a tool for organizing modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	ta	A library can contain up to 16,000 modules.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	ta	Modules				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	ta	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	ta	Dialog Modules				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ta	Dialog modules contain dialog definitions, including the dialog box properties, the properties of each dialog element and the events assigned. Since a dialog module can only contain a single dialog, they are often referred to as "dialogs".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	ta	Information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	ta	You can set the locale used for controlling the formatting numbers, dates and currencies in $[officename] Basic in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>. In Basic format codes, the decimal point (\<emph\>.\</emph\>) is always used as \<emph\>placeholder\</emph\> for the decimal separator defined in your locale and will be replaced by the corresponding character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	ta	The same applies to the locale settings for date, time and currency formats. The Basic format code will be interpreted and displayed according to your locale setting.				20200411 15:09:53
