helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	ta	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial time number that is used to calculate the number of seconds.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	9			0	ta	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the seconds of a serial time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>functions. For example, the expression:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	ta	Print Second(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117				0	ta	returns the value 41.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	ta	Sub ExampleSecond				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	ta	MsgBox "The exact second of the current time is "& Second( Now )				20200411 15:09:53
