helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	$[officename] Basic Glossary				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Basic Glossary\"\>$[officename] Basic Glossary\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	ta	This glossary explains some technical terms that you may come across when working with $[officename] Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155133				0	ta	Decimal Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156443				0	ta	When converting numbers, $[officename] Basic uses the locale settings of the system for determining the type of decimal and thousand separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	ta	The behavior has an effect on both the implicit conversion ( 1 + "2.3" = 3.3 ) as well as the runtime function \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03102700.xhp\" name=\"IsNumeric\"\>IsNumeric\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155854				0	ta	Colors				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ta	In $[officename] Basic, colors are treated as long integer value. The return value of color queries is also always a long integer value. When defining properties, colors can be specified using their RGB code that is converted to a long integer value using the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010305.xhp\" name=\"RGB function\"\>RGB function\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ta	Measurement Units				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	ta	In $[officename] Basic, a \<emph\>method parameter\</emph\> or a \<emph\>property\</emph\> expecting unit information can be specified either as integer or long integer expression without a unit, or as a character string containing a unit. If no unit is passed to the method the default unit defined for the active document type will be used. If the parameter is passed as a character string containing a measurement unit, the default setting will be ignored. The default measurement unit for a document type can be set under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - (Document Type) - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145801				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>twips; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	ta	Twips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	ta	A twip is a screen-independent unit which is used to define the uniform position and size of screen elements on all display systems. A twip is 1/1440th of an inch or 1/20 of a printer's point. There are 1440 twips to an inch or about 567 twips to a centimeter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153159				0	ta	URL Notation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	ta	URLs (\<emph\>Uniform Resource Locators\</emph\>) are used to determine the location of a resource like a file in a file system, typically inside a network environment. A URL consists of a protocol specifier, a host specifier and a file and path specifier:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	ta	\<emph\>protocol\</emph\>://\<emph\>host.name\</emph\>/\<emph\>path/to/the/file.html\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3168612				0	ta	The most common usage of URLs is on the internet when specifying web pages. Example for protocols are \<emph\>http\</emph\>, \<emph\>ftp\</emph\>, or \<emph\>file\</emph\>. The \<emph\>file\</emph\> protocol specifier is used when referring to a file on the local file system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150324	110			0	ta	URL notation does not allow certain special characters to be used. These are either replaced by other characters or encoded. A slash (\<emph\>/\</emph\>) is used as a path separator. For example, a file referred to as \<emph\>C:\\My File.sxw\</emph\> on the local host in "Windows notation" becomes \<emph\>file:///C|/My%20File.sxw\</emph\> in URL notation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Blue Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149180				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>Blue function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010301.xhp\" name=\"Blue Function [Runtime]\"\>Blue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156343				0	ta	Returns the blue component of the specified color code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	ta	Blue (Color As Long)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	ta	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ta	Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	ta	Parameter:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150448				0	ta	\<emph\>Color value\</emph\>: Long integer expression that specifies any \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000003.xhp#farbcodes\" name=\"color code\"\>color code\</link\> for which to return the blue component.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153091				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	ta	Sub ExampleColor				20200411 15:09:53
