helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	ta	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154924				0	ta	\<emph\>Text\</emph\>: String that you want to right-align in the string variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	ta	\<emph\>Variable1:\</emph\> User-defined variable that is the target for the copied variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	ta	\<emph\>Variable2:\</emph\> User-defined variable that you want to copy to another variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ta	If the string is shorter than the string variable, \<emph\>RSet\</emph\> aligns the string to the right within the string variable. Any remaining characters in the string variable are replaced with spaces. If the string is longer than the string variable, characters exceeding the length of the variable are truncated, and only the remaining characters are right-aligned within the string variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	ta	You can also use the \<emph\>RSet statement\</emph\> to assign variables of one user-defined type to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	ta	The following example uses the \<emph\>RSet\</emph\> and \<emph\>LSet\</emph\> statements to modify the left and right alignment of a string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154909				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218				0	ta	Sub ExampleRLSet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3147288				0	ta	Dim sVar as string				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367				0	ta	Dim sExpr as string				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952				0	ta	sVar = String(40,"*")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	ta	sExpr = "SBX"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	ta	REM Right-align "SBX" in a 40-character string				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ta	REM Replace asterisks with spaces				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ta	RSet sVar = sExpr				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	ta	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ta	sVar = String(5,"*")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	ta	sExpr = "123457896"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	ta	RSet sVar = sExpr				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116				0	ta	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	ta	sVar = String(40,"*")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	ta	sExpr = "SBX"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ta	REM Left-align "SBX" in a 40-character string				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	ta	LSet sVar = sExpr				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511				0	ta	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3153839				0	ta	sVar = String(5,"*")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3149122				0	ta	sExpr = "123456789"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	ta	LSet sVar = sExpr				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120308.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	ta	Print ">"; sVar; "<"				20200411 15:09:53
