helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>If statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090101.xhp\" name=\"If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\"\>If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	ta	Defines one or more statement blocks that you only want to execute if a given condition is True.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	ta	If condition=true Then Statement block [ElseIf condition=true Then] Statement block [Else] Statement block EndIf\<br/\>Instead of Else If you can write ElseIf, instead of End If you can write EndIf.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	ta	The \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement executes program blocks depending on given conditions. When $[officename] Basic encounters an \<emph\>If\</emph\> statement, the condition is tested. If the condition is True, all subsequent statements up to the next \<emph\>Else\</emph\> or \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement are executed. If the condition is False, and an \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement follows, $[officename] Basic tests the next condition and executes the following statements if the condition is True. If False, the program continues either with the next \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> or \<emph\>Else\</emph\> statement. Statements following \<emph\>Else\</emph\> are executed only if none of the previously tested conditions were True. After all conditions are evaluated, and the corresponding statements executed, the program continues with the statement following \<emph\>EndIf\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ta	You can nest multiple \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statements.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ta	\<emph\>Else\</emph\> and \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statements are optional.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152939				0	ta	You can use \<emph\>GoTo\</emph\> and \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> to jump out of an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> block, but not to jump into an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	ta	The following example enables you to enter the expiration date of a product, and determines if the expiration date has passed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152576				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	ta	Sub ExampleIfThenDate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	ta	Dim sDate as String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ta	Dim sToday as String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ta	sDate = InputBox("Enter the expiration date (MM.DD.YYYY)")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	ta	sDate = Right$(sDate, 4) + Mid$(sDate, 4, 2) + Left$(sDate, 2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	ta	sToday = Date$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	ta	sToday = Right$(sToday, 4)+ Mid$(sToday, 4, 2) + Left$(sToday, 2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	ta	If sDate < sToday Then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601				0	ta	MsgBox "The expiration date has passed"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	ta	ElseIf sDate > sToday Then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146912				0	ta	MsgBox "The expiration date has not yet passed"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	ta	Else				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ta	MsgBox "The expiration date is today"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	ta	End If				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	ta	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	AND Operator [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146117				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>AND operator (logical)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146117				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03060100.xhp\" name=\"AND Operator [Runtime]\"\>AND Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143268				0	ta	Logically combines two expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	ta	Result = Expression1 And Expression2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	ta	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that records the result of the combination.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ta	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any expressions that you want to combine.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156215				0	ta	Boolean expressions combined with AND only return the value \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions evaluate to \<emph\>True\</emph\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	ta	\<emph\>True\</emph\> AND \<emph\>True\</emph\> returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>; for all other combinations the result is \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ta	The AND operator also performs a bitwise comparison of identically positioned bits in two numeric expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	ta	Sub ExampleAnd				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ta	Dim A as Variant, B as Variant, C as Variant, D as Variant				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	ta	Dim vVarOut as Variant				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	ta	A = 10: B = 8: C = 6: D = Null				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	ta	vVarOut = A > B And B > C REM returns -1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	ta	vVarOut = B > A And B > C REM returns 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	ta	vVarOut = A > B And B > D REM returns 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	ta	vVarOut = (B > D And B > A) REM returns 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	ta	vVarOut = B And A REM returns 8 due to the bitwise AND combination of both arguments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	ta	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Debugging a Basic Program				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153344				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>debugging Basic programs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables; observing values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>watching variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>run-time errors in Basic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error codes in Basic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breakpoints\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Call Stack window\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153344				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01030300.xhp\"\>Debugging a Basic Program\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159224				0	ta	Breakpoints and Single Step Execution				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150682				0	ta	You can check each line in your Basic program for errors using single step execution. Errors are easily traced since you can immediately see the result of each step. A pointer in the breakpoint column of the Editor indicates the current line. You can also set a breakpoint if you want to force the program to be interrupted at a specific position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	ta	Double-click in the \<emph\>breakpoint\</emph\> column at the left of the Editor window to toggle a breakpoint at the corresponding line. When the program reaches a breakpoint, the program execution is interrupted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	8			0	ta	The \<emph\>single step \</emph\>execution using the \<emph\>Single Step\</emph\> icon causes the program to branch into procedures and functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ta	The procedure step execution using the \<emph\>Procedure Step\</emph\> icon causes the program to skip over procedures and functions as a single step.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	ta	Properties of a Breakpoint				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147574				0	ta	The properties of a breakpoint are available through its context menu by right-clicking the breakpoint in the breakpoint column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	10			0	ta	You can \<emph\>activate\</emph\> and \<emph\>deactivate\</emph\> a breakpoint by selecting \<emph\>Active\</emph\> from its context menu. When a breakpoint is deactivated, it does not interrupt the program execution. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ta	Select \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> from the context menu of a breakpoint or select \<emph\>Breakpoints\</emph\> from the context menu of the breakpoint column to call the \<emph\>Breakpoints\</emph\> dialog where you can specify other breakpoint options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ta	The list displays all \<emph\>breakpoints\</emph\> with the corresponding line number in the source code. You can activate or deactivate a selected breakpoint by checking or clearing the \<emph\>Active\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	ta	The \<emph\>Pass Count\</emph\> specifies the number of times the breakpoint can be passed over before the program is interrupted. If you enter 0 (default setting) the program is always interrupted as soon as a breakpoint is encountered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> to remove the breakpoint from the program.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	ta	Observing the Value of Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	ta	You can monitor the values of a variable by adding it to the \<emph\>Watch\</emph\> window. To add a variable to the list of watched variables, type the variable name in the \<emph\>Watch\</emph\> text box and press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	ta	The values of variables are only displayed if they are in scope. Variables that are not defined at the current source code location display ("Out of Scope") instead of a value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ta	You can also include arrays in the Watch window. If you enter the name of an array variable without an index value in the Watch text box, the content of the entire array is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	ta	If you rest the mouse over a predefined variable in the Editor at run-time, the content of the variable is displayed in a pop-up box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148618				0	ta	The Call Stack Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BASICIDE_STACKWINDOW_LIST\"\>Provides an overview of the call hierarchy of procedures and functions.\</ahelp\> You can determine which procedures and functions called which other procedures and functions at the current point in the source code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150594				0	ta	List of Run-Time Errors				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	RmDir Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148947				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>RmDir statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148947				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020413.xhp\" name=\"RmDir Statement [Runtime]\"\>RmDir Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	ta	Deletes an existing directory from a data medium.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	ta	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	ta	RmDir Text As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	ta	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies the name and path of the directory that you want to delete. You can also use \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/00000002.xhp\" name=\"URL notation\"\>URL notation\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ta	If the path is not determined, the \<emph\>RmDir Statement\</emph\> searches for the directory that you want to delete in the current path. If it is not found there, an error message appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145271				0	ta	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	ta	Sub ExampleRmDir				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020413.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ta	MkDir "C:\\Test2"				20200411 15:09:53
