helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	ta	Result = Expression1 Or Expression2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151211				0	ta	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ta	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that contains the result of the disjunction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229				0	ta	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any numeric expressions that you want to compare.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ta	A logical OR disjunction of two Boolean expressions returns the value True if at least one comparison expression is True.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ta	A bit-wise comparison sets a bit in the result if the corresponding bit is set in at least one of the two expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
