helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	ta	The following examples are for a new \<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/create_dialog.xhp\" name=\"dialog\"\>dialog\</link\> called "Dialog1". Use the tools on the \<emph\>Toolbox\</emph\> bar in the dialog editor to create the dialog and add the following controls: a \<emph\>Check Box\</emph\> called "CheckBox1", a \<emph\>Label Field\</emph\> called "Label1", a \<emph\>Button\</emph\> called "CommandButton1", and a \<emph\>List Box\</emph\> called "ListBox1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154141				0	ta	Be consistent with uppercase and lowercase letter when you attach a control to an object variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154909				0	ta	Global Function for Loading Dialogs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	ta	Function LoadDialog(Libname as String, DialogName as String, Optional oLibContainer)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	ta	Dim oLib as Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ta	Dim oLibDialog as Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ta	Dim oRuntimeDialog as Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	ta	If IsMissing(oLibContainer ) then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	ta	oLibContainer = DialogLibraries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	ta	End If				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	ta	oLibContainer.LoadLibrary(LibName)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ta	oLib = oLibContainer.GetByName(Libname)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	ta	oLibDialog = oLib.GetByName(DialogName)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ta	oRuntimeDialog = CreateUnoDialog(oLibDialog)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ta	LoadDialog() = oRuntimeDialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ta	End Function				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149412				0	ta	Displaying a Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ta	rem global definition of variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	ta	Dim oDialog1 AS Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	ta	Sub StartDialog1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913				0	ta	BasicLibraries.LoadLibrary("Tools")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	ta	oDialog1 = LoadDialog("Standard", "Dialog1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155767				0	ta	oDialog1.Execute()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	ta	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	ta	Read or Edit Properties of Controls in the Program				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	ta	Sub Sample1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	ta	BasicLibraries.LoadLibrary("Tools")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	ta	oDialog1 = LoadDialog("Standard", "Dialog1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232				0	ta	REM get dialog model				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3146316				0	ta	oDialog1Model = oDialog1.Model				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154021				0	ta	REM display text of Label1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	ta	oLabel1 = oDialog1.GetControl("Label1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3152584				0	ta	MsgBox oLabel1.Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	ta	REM set new text for control Label1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154119				0	ta	oLabel1.Text = "New Files"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155115				0	ta	REM display model properties for the control CheckBox1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	ta	oCheckBox1Model = oDialog1Model.CheckBox1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153270				0	ta	MsgBox oCheckBox1Model.Dbg_Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149817				0	ta	REM set new state for CheckBox1 for model of control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3145134				0	ta	oCheckBox1Model.State = 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3159102				0	ta	REM display model properties for control CommandButton1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	ta	oCMD1Model = oDialog1Model.CommandButton1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	ta	MsgBox oCMD1Model.Dbg_Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150368				0	ta	REM display properties of control CommandButton1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	ta	oCMD1 = oDialog1.GetControl("CommandButton1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	ta	MsgBox oCMD1.Dbg_Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	ta	REM execute dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154485				0	ta	oDialog1.Execute()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3146115				0	ta	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145387				0	ta	Add an Entry to a ListBox				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155088				0	ta	Sub AddEntry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154528				0	ta	BasicLibraries.LoadLibrary("Tools")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3159222				0	ta	oDialog1 = LoadDialog("Standard", "Dialog1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	ta	REM adds a new entry to the ListBox				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	ta	oDialog1Model = oDialog1.Model				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	ta	oListBox = oDialog1.GetControl("ListBox1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ta	dim iCount as integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3151243				0	ta	iCount = oListbox.ItemCount				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3144504				0	ta	oListbox.additem("New Item" & iCount,0)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149328				0	ta	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147071				0	ta	Remove an Entry from a ListBox				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3159095				0	ta	Sub RemoveEntry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3154958				0	ta	BasicLibraries.LoadLibrary("Tools")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3149443				0	ta	oDialog1 = LoadDialog("Standard", "Dialog1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153247				0	ta	REM remove the first entry from the ListBox				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302				0	ta	oDialog1Model = oDialog1.Model				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3153976				0	ta	oListBox = oDialog1.GetControl("ListBox1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3155383				0	ta	oListbox.removeitems(0,1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\sample_code.xhp	0	help	par_id3150892				0	ta	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Translation of Controls in the Dialog Editor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	bm_id8915372				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>dialogs;translating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>localizing dialogs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>translating dialogs\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3574896				0	ta	\<variable id=\"translation\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/translation.xhp\"\>Translation of Controls in the Dialog Editor\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4601940				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Language toolbar in the Basic IDE dialog editor shows controls to enable and manage localizable dialogs.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id9538560				0	ta	By default, any dialog that you create only contains string resources for one language. You may want to create dialogs that automatically show localized strings according to the user's language settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the language for the strings that you want to edit. Click the Manage Languages icon to add languages.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id71413				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a language, then click Default to set the language as default, or click Delete to remove the language from the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog where you can add a language to the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a language in the list and click Delete to remove that language. When you remove all languages, the string resources for localizable dialogs are removed from all dialogs in the current library.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a language in the list and click Default to set the language as default language.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The default language will be used as a source for all other language strings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Add UI languages for your dialog strings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6596881				0	ta	To enable localizable dialogs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	ta	In the Basic IDE dialog editor, open the Language toolbar choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Language\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	ta	If the current library already contains a localizable dialog, the Language toolbar is shown automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Manage Languages\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id2526017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_managelanguage.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2526017\"\>Manage Language icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Language toolbar or on the Toolbox bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	ta	You see the Manage User Interface Language dialog. The dialog manages languages for the current library. The name of the current library is shown on the title bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	ta	Click Add in the dialog to add a language entry. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	ta	This step enables all new dialogs to contain localizable string resources.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	ta	The first time you click Add, you see the Set Default User Interface Language dialog. The following times you click Add, this dialog has the name Add User Interface Language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	ta	You can also change the default language in the Manage User Interface Language dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	ta	Select a language. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	ta	This adds string resources to contain the translated versions of all strings to the dialog properties. The set of dialog strings of the default language is copied to the new set of strings. Later, you can switch to the new language and then translate the strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	ta	Close the dialog or add additional languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	hd_id631733				0	ta	To edit localizable controls in your dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	ta	Once you have added the resources for localizable strings in your dialogs, you can select the current language from the Current Language listbox on the Language toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	ta	Switch the Current Language listbox to display the default language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	ta	Insert any number of controls to your dialog and enter all strings you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	ta	Select another language in the Current Language listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	ta	Using the control's property dialogs, edit all strings to the other language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	ta	Repeat for all languages that you added.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	ta	The user of your dialog will see the strings of the user interface language of the user's version of %PRODUCTNAME, if you did provide strings in that language. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	ta	If no language matches the user's version, the user will see the default language strings. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\translation.xhp	0	help	par_id3050325				0	ta	If the user has an older version of %PRODUCTNAME that does not know localizable string resources for Basic dialogs, the user will see the default language strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Opening a Dialog With Program Code				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154140				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>module/dialog toggle\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dialogs;using program code to show (example)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples; showing a dialog using program code\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154140				0	ta	\<variable id=\"show_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/show_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Opening a Dialog With Program Code\"\>Opening a Dialog With Program Code\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> BASIC window for a dialog that you created, leave the dialog editor by clicking the name tab of the Module that the dialog is assigned to. The name tab is at the bottom of the window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	ta	Enter the following code for a subroutine called \<emph\>Dialog1Show\</emph\>. In this example, the name of the dialog that you created is "Dialog1":				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156443				0	ta	Sub Dialog1Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ta	BasicLibraries.LoadLibrary("Tools")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	ta	oDialog1 = \<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/sample_code.xhp\" name=\"LoadDialog\"\>LoadDialog\</link\>("Standard", "Dialog1")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	ta	oDialog1.Execute()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349				0	ta	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	ta	Without using "LoadDialog" you can call the code as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	ta	Sub Dialog1Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	ta	DialogLibraries.LoadLibrary( "Standard" )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	ta	oDialog1 = CreateUnoDialog( DialogLibraries.Standard.Dialog1 )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	ta	oDialog1.Execute()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	ta	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\show_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	ta	When you execute this code, "Dialog1" opens. To close the dialog, click the close button (x) on its title bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\insert_control.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Creating Controls in the Dialog Editor				20200411 15:09:53
