helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Print File Directly				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialog, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	ta	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	ta	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	AutoFilter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149495				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>AutoFilter\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFilter\"\>Filters the records, based on the content of the currently selected data field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3147261\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147261\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043				0	ta	AutoFilter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	ta	Place the cursor in a field name whose content you want to filter and then click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon. Only those records with content identical to the selected field name are visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159234				0	ta	For example, to view all the customers from New York, click a field name with the entry "New York". AutoFilter then filters all customers from New York from the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577				0	ta	You can remove the current AutoFilter with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\> icon or with \<emph\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	ta	To filter with several field names simultaneously, click the \<emph\>Default Filter \</emph\>icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter dialog\"\>Default Filter\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can combine several filter criteria.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Table Element Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150620				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170800.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard\"\>Table Element Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155354				0	ta	If you insert a table control in a document, the \<emph\>Table Element Wizard\</emph\> starts automatically. In this wizard, you can interactively specify which information is displayed in the table control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154422				0	ta	You can use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>\<emph\>Wizards On/Off\</emph\>\</link\> icon to keep the wizard from starting automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
