helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147000				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>sorting; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; sorting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sortierung\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort Order\"\>Sort Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163829				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sortierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort criteria for the data display.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149549	12			0	ta	While the functions \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Ascending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Ascending Order\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Descending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Descending Order\</emph\>\</link\> sort by one criterion only, you can combine several criteria in the\<emph\> Sort Order \</emph\>dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	ta	You can remove a sorting that has been performed with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</emph\>\</link\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148548				0	ta	Sorting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	ta	Use this area to enter sorting criteria. If you enter additional sorting criteria under \<emph\>and then\</emph\>, the data matching the content of the higher-order criterion is ordered according to the next criterion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148620				0	ta	If you sort the field name "First name" in ascending order and the field name "last name" in descending order, all records will be sorted in ascending order by first name, and then within the first names, in descending order by last name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ta	Field name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the data field name whose content will determine the sort order.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	ta	Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort order (either ascending or descending).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	ta	and then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ta	Specifies additional subordinate sort criteria from the other fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Special Tips for Date Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	ta	Special Tips for Date Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	ta	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	ta	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document.				20200411 15:09:53
