helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149999				0	ta	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" id=\"img_id3146130\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146130\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	ta	Apply Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226	4			0	ta	The\<emph\> Apply Filter \</emph\>function retains \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"form-based filters\"\>form-based filters\</link\> that have been set. You do not need to redefine them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Control Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147102				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of form controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties; form controls\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147102				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ta	\<variable id=\"kontroll\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlProperties\"\>Opens a dialog for editing the properties of a selected control.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3157910	17			0	ta	\<variable id=\"hinweis\"\>You can only call the\<emph\> Properties\</emph\> dialog when in the Design mode with a control selected. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760				0	ta	If you enter data in the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog, note that multiline input is possible for certain drop-down combo boxes. This concerns all fields in which an SQL statement can be entered, as well as the properties of text boxes or label fields. You can open these fields and enter text in the opened list. The following shortcut keys are valid:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	ta	Keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	ta	Effects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150944				0	ta	Opens the combo box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153063				0	ta	Closes the combo box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ta	Shift+Enter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ta	Inserts a new line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	ta	Up Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ta	Places the cursor into the previous line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ta	Down Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ta	Places the cursor into the next line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178				0	ta	Enter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	ta	Completes the input in the field and places the cursor into the next field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ta	As with list boxes or combo boxes, you can open or close the list with a mouse click at the arrow on the right end of the field. However, the input here can be entered either in the opened list or in the top text field. An exception is the properties that expect a list representation, for example, the property \<emph\>List Entries\</emph\>, which can be set for the control fields \<emph\>List Box\</emph\> and \<emph\>Combo Box\</emph\>. Here, you can only edit the entries when the field is opened.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Special properties of a formatted field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	ta	Special properties of a formatted field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	ta	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	ta	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	ta	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ta	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Sort Descending				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154689				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>Sort Descending\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	2			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDown\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in descending order.\</ahelp\>Text fields are sorted alphabetically, number fields are sorted by number.				20200411 15:09:53
