helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946				0	ta	Imported data are treated as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ta	Date (DMY)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434				0	ta	Applies a date format (Day, Month, Year) to the imported data in a column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148740				0	ta	Date (MDY)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149688				0	ta	Applies a date format (Month, Day, Year) to the imported data in a column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	ta	Date (YMD)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153207				0	ta	Applies a date format (Year, Month, Day) to the imported data in a column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148981				0	ta	US English				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178				0	ta	Numbers formatted in US English are searched for and included regardless of the system language. A number format is not applied. If there are no US English entries, the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> format is applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3154329				0	ta	Hide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3154946				0	ta	The data in the column are not imported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	ta	If you selected one of the date formats (DMY), (MDY), or (YMD) and you enter numbers without date delimiters, the numbers are interpreted as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650	76			0	ta	Number of characters 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495				0	ta	Date format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	ta	6				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056				0	ta	Two characters each are taken for day, month, and year in the selected order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352				0	ta	8				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ta	Four characters are taken for the year, two each for month and day, in the selected order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ta	5 or 7				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	ta	As with 6 or 8 characters, but the first part of the sequence has one character less. This will suppress a leading zero for month and day.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	ta	If you want to include the leading zero in the data you import, in telephone numbers for example, apply the "Text" format to the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287				0	ta	Preview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377				0	ta	Shows how the imported text will look after it is separated into columns. To apply a format to a column when it is imported, click a column and select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>. When you select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>, the column heading displays the applied format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ta	If you want to use a fixed width to separate the imported data into columns, click in the ruler to set the width boundaries.				20200411 15:09:53
