helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/07/09000000.xhp\" name=\"Web Pages\"\>Web Pages\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	ta	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	ta	A tool for creating new web pages is the Web Layout mode, which you enable with \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	ta	Creating a New Web Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	ta	Switch to the web layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	ta	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types.				20200411 15:09:53
