helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>queries;creating in SQL view\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>commands;SQL\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ta	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ta	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	ta	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	ta	To execute an SQL statement directly				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	ta	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbaexecutesql.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				20200411 15:09:53
