helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ta	\<variable id=\"floating_toolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/floating_toolbar.xhp\" name=\"Using Toolbars\"\>Using Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ta	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	ta	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	ta	Context of Toolbars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	ta	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	ta	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	ta	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id1905575				0	ta	To Close a Toolbar Permanently				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id9776909				0	ta	While the toolbar is visible, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar to remove the check mark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	ta	To Show a Closed Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id7296975				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Reset\</emph\> to reset the toolbars to their default context sensitive behavior. Now some toolbars will be shown automatically, dependent on the context.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E9				0	ta	To Make a Toolbar a Floating Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	ta	Click the handle at the start of the toolbar, and drag the toolbar into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	ta	To Reattach a Floating Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F7				0	ta	Drag the title bar of the toolbar to an edge of the document window. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id6154362				0	ta	To reattach a floating window, drag-and-drop the window's title bar to an edge of the document window. The mouse pointer should be very close to the document window's edge when you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id1510055				0	ta	Depending on your system's window manager settings, you may also double-click an empty place on the toolbar or window, while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. Or double-click the title bar of the floating toolbar or window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AC				0	ta	Docking toolbars and windows by drag-and-drop depends on your system's window manager settings. You must enable your system to show the full window contents when you move a window, instead of showing just the outer frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Creating Reports 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ta	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ta	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Builder window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	ta	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	ta	Report Builder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	ta	Report Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	ta	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	ta	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	ta	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	ta	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	ta	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9869075				0	ta	Select from several given choices to arrange the data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8611713				0	ta	Generates a one-time snapshot of the data. To see an updated report, execute the same report again to create a Writer document with the updated data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2866908				0	ta	You can choose to generate a one-time snapshot with fixed data, or a "live" report with links to the current data at the time when you open the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4169743				0	ta	Saves the report as a Writer text document. Stores the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id408948				0	ta	Saves the report and the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2891933				0	ta	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to create a new report with the current data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id6142765				0	ta	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to either see again the static snapshot of the data from first creation time, or to create a new report with the current data. This depends on your choice on the last page of the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1757560				0	ta	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to open the Report Builder window, with the report's information loaded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4649189				0	ta	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to edit the Writer template file that was used to create the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	hd_id8414258				0	ta	Creating a New Report Manually In Design View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id3119602				0	ta	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4226508				0	ta	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5758842				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Create Report in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	ta	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	ta	Creating a New Report With the Report Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DC				0	ta	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	ta	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E8				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Report\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8032166				0	ta	Follow the steps of the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\> to create the report.				20200411 15:09:53
