helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Recording and Displaying Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Track Changes, see review function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	ta	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	ta	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	ta	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ta	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	ta	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ta	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ta	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting Data From Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>sending; AutoAbstract function in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoAbstract function for sending text to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines; sending to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; copying by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; copying and pasting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152924				0	ta	\<variable id=\"copytext2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytext2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Text Documents\"\>Inserting Data From Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	ta	You can insert text into other document types, such as spreadsheets and presentations. Note that there is a difference between whether the text is inserted into a text frame, a spreadsheet cell, or into the outline view of a presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ta	If you copy text to the clipboard, you can paste it with or without text attributes. Use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V to paste.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3143270\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paste.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143270\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ta	To select the format in which the clipboard contents will be pasted, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>, then select the proper format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	ta	If a text document contains headings formatted with the Heading Paragraph Style, choose \<emph\>File - Send - Outline to Presentation\</emph\>. A new presentation document is created, which contains the headings as an outline.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	ta	If you want to transfer each heading together with its accompanying paragraphs, select the \<emph\>File - Send - AutoAbstract to Presentation\</emph\> command. You must have formatted the headings with a corresponding Paragraph Style to be able to see this command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	ta	Copying Text Using Drag-and-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	ta	If you select text and drag it into a spreadsheet with drag-and-drop, it will be inserted as text into the cell where you release the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	ta	If you drag text to the normal view of a presentation, an OLE object is inserted as a $[officename] plug-in.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	ta	If you drag the text to the outline view of a presentation, it will be inserted at the cursor location.				20200411 15:09:53
