helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	ta	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	ta	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ta	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	ta	Creating a New Table View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	ta	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				20200411 15:09:53
