helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ta	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ta	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	ta	To register an existing database file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	ta	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	ta	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	ta	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	ta	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	ta	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting Hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ta	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ta	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	ta	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	ta	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ta	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	ta	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	ta	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	ta	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	ta	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	ta	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ta	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	ta	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	ta	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ta	Select the drawing object or objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	ta	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	ta	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	ta	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	ta	Inserting into a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	ta	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	ta	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	ta	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Configuring $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>configuring; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ta	\<variable id=\"configure_overview\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/configure_overview.xhp\" name=\"Configuring $[officename]\"\>Configuring $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ta	You can customize your $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ta	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog to change toolbars, menus and other user interface items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	ta	You are free to change the items on the menu bar. You can delete items, add new ones, copy items from one menu to another, rename them, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ta	The toolbars may be freely configured.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	ta	You can change the shortcut keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3153345				0	ta	You can change default settings of $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	optid3155421				0	ta	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/010000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> dialog to change a variety of settings you will use in $[officename] modules. Items presented in the \<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\> menu will change depending on the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3145071				0	ta	In \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find options for your default language and currency setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3149811				0	ta	In \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] Writer - Basic Fonts\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find default font settings. Change these to suit your preferences. Fonts can easily be changed on per document basis.				20200411 15:09:53
