helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	ta	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	ta	To Add a Button to a Document 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ta	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	ta	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ta	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	ta	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	ta	Specify the properties of the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	ta	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	ta	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	ta	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	ta	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	ta	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	ta	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	ta	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	ta	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	ta	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ta	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ta	Click one of the predefined border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	ta	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	ta	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ta	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ta	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	ta	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ta	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	ta	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ta	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	ta	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ta	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ta	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ta	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	ta	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ta	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ta	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ta	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ta	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ta	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ta	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ta	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ta	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	ta	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	ta	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	ta	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id2182378				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Editing Graphic Objects 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings, see also draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphic objects, see draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	ta	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ta	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	ta	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Draw multiple objects of the same type. Click the document without moving the mouse to stop drawing objects.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	ta	If you want to open up draw objects from the center instead of dragging from one corner to the other, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With some window managers, you may need to hold down also the meta key.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	ta	Holding down the Shift key while dragging restricts the created object. For example, instead of a rectangle you get a square, instead of an ellipse you get a circle. When you drag a handle of an existing object with Shift held down, the aspect ratio of the object is retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	ta	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id224616				0	ta	To scale a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab repeatedly to highlight one of the handles. Then press an arrow key. To scale in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key. Press Esc to leave the point edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	ta	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the Shift key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7199316				0	ta	To move a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press an arrow key. To move in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7133399316				0	ta	To enter text to be a part of a graphics object, select the object and start typing your text. Click outside the object to end entering text. Double-click text inside an object to edit the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ta	To revert to normal mode after creating and editing draw objects, click in an area of the document containing no objects. If you see a drawing cursor, first exit this mode by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
