helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	ta	\<variable id=\"language_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Document Language\"\>Selecting the Document Language\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ta	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	ta	The language you select applies to the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	ta	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	ta	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	ta	Selecting a language for the whole document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>. Go to \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>\<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ta	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152938				0	ta	Selecting a language for a Paragraph Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	ta	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	ta	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	ta	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	ta	Applying a language directly to selected text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	ta	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	ta	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	ta	Selecting a language for a Character Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	ta	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	ta	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	ta	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	ta	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id8703268				0	ta	Adding More Text Languages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7919248				0	ta	Dictionaries are supplied and installed as extensions. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Language - More Dictionaries Online\</item\> to open the dictionaries page in your default web browser.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id5174108				0	ta	Select a dictionary in the list of descriptions. Click the heading in a dictionary description that you want to get.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2897427				0	ta	In the next page, click the Get It icon to download the dictionary extension. Note the folder name to which your browser downloads the file. Download additional dictionaries as you like.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3906979				0	ta	In %PRODUCTNAME, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> and click Add to install the downloaded extensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id0220200911174493				0	ta	After you installed the extensions, you should close %PRODUCTNAME (including the Quickstarter), and restart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9100924				0	ta	Setting UI Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ta	A standard installation of %PRODUCTNAME software will give you a user interface (UI) of your chosen language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ta	Most users download the American English version, which gives you English menu commands and English application help. If you want another language for the menus (and for the application help, if available in that language), change the UI language as follows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ta	Select another UI language in the "User interface" listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ta	Click OK and restart the %PRODUCTNAME software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ta	If the listbox doesn't list the language that you want, see "Adding More UI Languages".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	ta	Adding More UI Languages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ta	Open your Web browser and enter \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\"\>https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ta	Select and download the correct language pack for your version of %PRODUCTNAME software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ta	Close %PRODUCTNAME software (also close the Quickstarter, if you enabled it).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ta	Install the language pack. Either double-click the exe file, or unpack the tar.gz file according to standard practice on your platform.				20200411 15:09:53
