helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571				0	ta	\<variable id=\"dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\"\>Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ta	There are many options for moving or copying objects using drag-and-drop. Text sections, drawing objects, graphics, form controls, hyperlinks, cell ranges, and many more can be moved or copied with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ta	Note that the mouse pointer displays a plus sign when copying and an arrow when creating a link or hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
