helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	ta	Copying				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/helpimg/linkdata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Mouse pointer inserting link\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	ta	Creating a link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ta	If you press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while releasing the mouse button, you can control whether the object is copied, moved, or a link is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3158407\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3158407\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ta	If you drag objects out of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>\<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>\</link\>, you can specify in the submenu of the Navigator's \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon whether to copy the object, insert it as a link or insert it as a hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	ta	You can cancel a drag-and-drop operation in $[officename] at any time by pressing the Esc key before releasing the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Adding Texture to Chart Bars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>charts; bars with textures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>textures;on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;textures on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	ta	\<variable id=\"chart_barformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_barformat.xhp\" name=\"Adding Texture to Chart Bars\"\>Adding Texture to Chart Bars\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	ta	You can add texture to the bars in a graph or chart (instead of the default colors) via bitmap graphics:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ta	Enter edit mode by double-clicking on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ta	Click on any bar of the bar series you want to edit. All bars of this series are now selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id720847				0	ta	If you want to edit only one bar, click again on that bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ta	In the context menu choose \<emph\>Object Properties\</emph\>. Then choose the \<emph\>Area\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ta	Click on \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>. In the list box select a bitmap as a texture for the currently selected bars. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to accept the setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Printing Address Labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ta	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	ta	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab page, select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370863				0	ta	Choose the database and table from which to get the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id013020090337089				0	ta	Select a database field of which you want to print the contents. Click the button that shows a left arrow to insert the database field into the Label Text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370930				0	ta	Continue to select and insert database fields if you want more fields on every label. You can press Enter to insert a new line, and you can type any character to insert fixed text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370924				0	ta	Optionally, if you want to type more text, apply formatting, or insert images and line art, you should enable \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. If you enable this, once you leave the Labels dialog box a small window opens with a Synchronize button. Now you only need to work on the first label on the labels document, then click the Synchronize button to copy your work to every label of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	ta	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ta	When you see the label document, you might want to temporarily enable \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Field Names\</item\>. This displays the fields in a more visible manner, so that you can arrange and edit label contents more easily.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	ta	You can save and/or print the label document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id8476821				0	ta	When you choose to print the document, you will be asked if you want to print a form letter. Answer Yes to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialog. In the Mail Merge dialog, you can select the records for which you want to print labels.				20200411 15:09:53
