helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	ta	To move several tab stops on the ruler, press the Shift key before you click a tab. Drag one tab while continuing to press Shift to move that tab as well as all the tabs to the right of it. The spacing between those tabs remains the same.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349	23			0	ta	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you drag a tab on the ruler to move that tab and all the tabs to the right of it. This results in the spacing between those tabs changing proportionally to their distance from the margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146				0	ta	Changing the Properties of Tabs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	ta	To change tab type, click the tab you want to change on the ruler, then right-click to open the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	ta	Deleting Tabs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148879				0	ta	To delete a tab, hold down the mouse button while you drag the tab outside the ruler.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151074				0	ta	Changing the Defaults				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3151059				0	ta	If you want to change the settings of your default tab stops, you will find further information under \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>(module name) - General\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the Options dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	ta	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the ruler allows you to change the displayed units of measurement. These changes are only valid until you exit $[officename], and they only apply to the ruler on whose context menu you made the change. If you want to change the ruler measurement units permanently, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - [Document type] - View\</emph\> and change the measurement unit there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148429				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Ruler\"\>Ruler\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
