helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	ta	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	ta	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	ta	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	ta	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace \</emph\>dialog changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	ta	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	ta	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	ta	To search for all font changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	ta	Clear the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box if necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> check box, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog, you now can read "Font" below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	ta	All places where a font change was applied, either directly or by assigning an appropriate style, are found.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FE				0	ta	To reset the Find & Replace mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	ta	To stop searching for the current attributes, reset the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog to normal mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	ta	Click \<emph\>No Format\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id6837672				0	ta	Searching for attributes is available in the Find & Replace dialog for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Error Report Tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	ta	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ta	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ta	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	ta	Starting the Error Report Tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ta	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	ta	Completing the Report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	ta	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	ta	Sending the Error Report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	ta	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	ta	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ta	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ta	What Data is Sent?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ta	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	ta	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ta	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ta	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ta	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	ta	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ta	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	ta	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Working with Queries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	bm_id840784				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;data in databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;defining (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;database queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Query Wizard (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	ta	\<variable id=\"data_queries\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_queries.xhp\"\>Working with Queries\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	ta	If you often want to access only a subset of your data that can be well defined by a filter condition, you can define a query. This is basically a name for the new view at the filtered data. You open the query and see the current data in the table layout that you defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	ta	Creating a New Query With the Query Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	ta	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new query using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard00.xhp\"\>Query Wizard\</link\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	ta	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	ta	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Query\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	ta	Creating a New Query With the Design View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	ta	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	ta	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Create Query in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ta	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	ta	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ta	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	ta	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	ta	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	ta	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	ta	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	ta	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	ta	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	ta	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	ta	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	ta	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	ta	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	ta	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	ta	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	ta	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	ta	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	ta	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	ta	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	ta	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	ta	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	ta	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id6426892				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating and Testing XML filters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
