helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	ta	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ta	Place the cursor in the paragraph for which you want to define a border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	ta	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ta	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ta	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149237				0	ta	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	ta	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	ta	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ta	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	ta	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	ta	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	ta	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ta	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	ta	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ta	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ta	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	ta	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	ta	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	ta	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Comparing Versions of a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;document versions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	ta	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	ta	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	ta	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	ta	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ta	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	ta	Open the reviewer's document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	ta	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	ta	A file selection dialog appears. Select your older original document and confirm the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ta	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into the reviewer's document. All text passages that occur in the reviewer's document but not in the original are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that got deleted by the reviewer are identified as deletions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	ta	You can now accept or reject the insertions and deletions. At the end you may save the reviewer's document as a new original with a new name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	ta	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	ta	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	ta	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	ta	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	ta	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	ta	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	ta	Select one of the options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	ta	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	ta	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	ta	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	ta	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	ta	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	ta	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	ta	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME features\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	ta	\<variable id=\"accessibility\"\>\<link name=\"Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME\" href=\"text/shared/guide/accessibility.xhp\"\>Accessibility in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3154894				0	ta	The following accessibility features are part of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	ta	Support of \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"external devices and applications\"\>external devices and applications\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	ta	Access to all functions by keyboard. The keys that replace the mouse actions are listed in the \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME Help\" href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	ta	Improved readability of screen contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ta	Zooming of on-screen user interface for menus, icons, and documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	ta	The user interface is scalable through your \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Window Manager\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>operating system\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> settings. The default font size for dialogs is 12pt, corresponding to a scale of 100%. You can also change the font size for dialogs in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</emph\>. The zoom factor of a document can be changed in \<emph\>View - Zoom\</emph\>, or by double-clicking the zoom factor displayed in the Status Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	ta	Please note that accessibility support relies on Java technology for communications with assistive technology tools. This means that the first program startup may take a few seconds longer, because the Java runtime environment has to be started as well.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - View\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Appearance\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	ta	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Accessibility\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Mobile Device Filters for Pocket Device Appliances 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147143				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>mobile device filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pocket device appliances\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;mobile device filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Palm file filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Pocket PC file filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;documents for mobile devices\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;mobile device documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;Pocket PC formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;Pocket PC and $[officename] formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;mobile device filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file filters;mobile devices\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147143				0	ta	\<variable id=\"mobiledevicefilters\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/mobiledevicefilters.xhp\" name=\"Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\"\>Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ta	You can save and open documents to and from several mobile devices file formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ta	Currently the following filters are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ta	AportisDoc for Palm OS compatible devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ta	Pocket Excel for Pocket PC compatible devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ta	Pocket Word for Pocket PC compatible devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	ta	Installing the Pocket PC filters under Windows will also install a DLL file that supports the synchronization software of your Pocket PC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	ta	The Java Runtime Environment is required to use the mobile device filters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665				0	ta	Installing the mobile device filters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ta	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	ta	If you are using the Windows operating system with ActiveSync installed, disconnect any Pocket PC device from ActiveSync.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	ta	Start the $[officename] Setup program:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	ta	Open the Windows \<emph\>Start\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>, double-click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION entry, click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	ta	In Setup, choose the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ta	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry, then open the \<emph\>Mobile Device Filters\</emph\> entry. Select the filters you want to install.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Install\</emph\>, \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to install the filters and exit the Setup program.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123				0	ta	Saving $[officename] documents for a mobile device				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	ta	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	ta	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	ta	Opening mobile device documents in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	ta	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	ta	Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159196				0	ta	Synchronizing file types				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ta	To convert Pocket PC formats to and from $[officename] formats, you must first change some options within ActiveSync. To do this, open the ActiveSync window and open its Options dialog. Perform the following steps:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	ta	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Conversion Settings\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
