helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_LISTBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_LB_RESULT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the headings of the pages found in your full-text search. To display a page, double-click its entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_FULLWORDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to carry out an exact search for the word you entered. Incomplete words will not be found.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_SCOPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to only search in document headings for the search term.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_SEARCH_PB_OPEN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the entry selected in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3152552				0	ta	The full text search function in $[officename] Help allows you to find Help documents that contain any combination of search terms. To do this, type one or more words into the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ta	The \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field stores the words you entered last. To repeat a previous search, click the arrow icon and select the term from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	ta	After the search has been carried out, the document headings of the results appear in a list. Either double-click an entry, or select it and click \<emph\>Display\</emph\> to load the corresponding Help document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	ta	Use the check box \<emph\>Find in headings only\</emph\> to limit the search to document headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	ta	The \<emph\>Complete words only\</emph\> check box allows you to perform an exact search. If this box is marked, incomplete words will not be found. Do not mark this check box if the search term you enter should also be found as part of a longer word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	ta	You can enter any combination of search terms, separated by spaces. Searching is not case-sensitive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	ta	The index and full-text searches always apply to the currently selected %PRODUCTNAME application. Select the appropriate application using the list box on the help viewer's toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
