helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10543				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard07.xhp\"\>Query Wizard - Aliases\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10553				0	ta	Assigns aliases to field names. Aliases are optional, and can provide more user-friendly names, which are displayed in place of field names. For example, an alias can be used when fields from different tables have the same name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	ta	Alias				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055A				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the alias for the field name.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055D				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard08.xhp\" name=\"Query Wizard - Overview\"\>Query Wizard - Overview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Missing Element				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>queries; missing elements (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	ta	Missing Element				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247	2			0	ta	If a query in which tables or fields no longer exist is opened, the\<emph\> Missing Element \</emph\>dialog appears. This dialog names the missing table or the field which cannot be interpreted and allows you to decide how to continue with the procedure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145072				0	ta	How to continue?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	ta	There are three options available for answering this question:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147576				0	ta	Do you really want to open the query in the graphic view?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3166461				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows you to open the query in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Design View\"\>Design View\</link\> in spite of missing elements.\</ahelp\> This option also allows you to specify if other errors need to be ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	ta	The query is opened in the Design View (the graphical interface). Missing tables appear blank and invalid fields appear with their (invalid) names in the list of fields. This lets you work with exactly those fields that caused the error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149578				0	ta	Open the query in the SQL View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows you to open the query design in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"SQL Mode\"\>SQL Mode\</link\> and to interpret the query as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/14030000.xhp\" name=\"Native SQL\"\>Native SQL\</link\>.\</ahelp\> You can only quit the native SQL mode when the $[officename] statement is completely interpreted (only possible if the used tables or fields in the query really exist).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	ta	Do not open the query				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows you to cancel the procedure and specify that the query should not be opened.\</ahelp\> This option corresponds to the function of the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> dialog button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148492				0	ta	Also ignore similar errors				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you selected the first option, but you still want to open the query in the graphics view in spite of missing elements, you can specify whether other errors are ignored.\</ahelp\> Therefore, in the current opening process, no error message will be displayed if the query can not be correctly interpreted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Relations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>Relations\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	2			0	ta	This command opens the \<emph\>Relation Design \</emph\>window, which allows you to define relationships between various database tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CTL_RELATIONTAB\"\>Here you can link together tables from the current database through common data fields.\</ahelp\> Click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon to create the relationships, or simply drag-and-drop with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	ta	This function is only available if you are working with a relational database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	ta	When you choose \<emph\>Tools - Relationships\</emph\>, a window opens in which all the existing relationships between the tables of the current database are shown. If no relationships have been defined, or if you want to relate other tables of the database to each other, then click the \<emph\>Add Tables\</emph\> icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/14020100.xhp\" name=\"Add Tables\"\>Add Tables\</link\> dialog opens in which you can select the tables that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152812				0	ta	If the \<emph\>Relation Design\</emph\> window is open, the selected tables cannot be modified, even in Table Design mode. This ensures that tables are not changed while the relations are being created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ta	The selected tables are shown in the top area of the design view. You can close a table window through the context menu or with the Delete key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148922				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>primary keys;inserting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keys;primary keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external keys (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148922				0	ta	Primary key and other key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168				0	ta	If you want to define a relation among the different tables, you should enter a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#primaerschluessel\" name=\"primary key\"\>primary key\</link\> that clearly identifies a data field of the existing table. You can refer to the primary key from other tables to access the data of this table. All data fields referring to this primary key will be identified as an external key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	ta	All data fields referring to a primary key will be identified in the table window by a small key symbol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	ta	Define relations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155430				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>relations; creating and deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	ta	All existing relations are shown in the relations windows by a line that connects the primary and other key fields. You can add a relation by using drag-and-drop to drop the field of one table onto the field of the other table. A relation is removed again by selecting it and pressing the Delete key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	ta	Alternatively, you can also click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon in the top area of the relation field and define the relation between two tables in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>\<emph\>Relations\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	ta	If you use $[officename] as the front-end for a relational database, the creation and deletion of relationships is not placed in an intermediate memory by $[officename], but is forwarded directly to the external database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856	15			0	ta	By double-clicking a connection line, you can assign certain properties to the relation. The \<emph\>Relations \</emph\>dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Table Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	bm_id6009094				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>wizards;database tables (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Table Wizard (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	par_idN1054C				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055C				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Table Wizard helps you to create a database table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\tablewizard00.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AF				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard01.xhp\" name=\"Table Wizard - Select fields\"\>Table Wizard - Select fields\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Join Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154015				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>links;relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inner joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>joins in databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>left joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>full joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154015				0	ta	Join Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151205				0	ta	If you double-click a connection between two linked fields in the query design, or if you choose \<emph\>Insert - New Relation\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Join Properties\</emph\> dialog appears. These properties will be used in all queries created in the future.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155066				0	ta	Tables involved				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_RIGHT_TABLE\"\>Specifies two different tables that you want to join.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	ta	Fields involved				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148994				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies two data fields that will be joined by a relation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159267				0	ta	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	ta	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>Specifies the link type of the selected link.\</ahelp\> Some databases support only a subset of the possible types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	ta	Inner Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the internal join, the results table contains only the records for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link is created by a corresponding WHERE clause.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	ta	Left Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the left join, the results table contains all fields of the left table and only those fields of the right table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the LEFT OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155607				0	ta	Right Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150647				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the right join, the results table contains all fields of the right table and only those fields of the left table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the RIGHT OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158215				0	ta	Full Join				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>For a full join, the results table contains all fields of the left and right tables.\</ahelp\> In the SQL of $[officename] this type of link corresponds to the FULL OUTER JOIN command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200912031976				0	ta	Natural				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912031977				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts the keyword NATURAL into the SQL statement that defines the relation. The relation joins all columns that have the same column name in both tables. The resulting joined table contains only one column for each pair of equally named columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Query Wizard - Grouping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10546				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard05.xhp\"\>Query Wizard - Grouping\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	ta	Specifies whether to group the query. The data source must support the SQL statement "Order by clauses" to enable this page of the Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10589				0	ta	Group by				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058D				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays all fields that are to be used to group the query.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard05.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard06.xhp\" name=\"Query Wizard - Grouping conditions\"\>Query Wizard - Grouping conditions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Query Wizard - Grouping Conditions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10546				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard06.xhp\"\>Query Wizard - Grouping Conditions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	ta	Specifies the conditions to group the query. The data source must support the SQL statement "Order by clauses" to enable this page of the Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10559				0	ta	Match all of the following				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055D				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select to group the query by all the conditions using a logical AND.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	ta	Match any of the following				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10564				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select to group the query by any of the conditions using a logical OR.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN10567				0	ta	Field name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\querywizard06.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056B				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the field name for the grouping condition.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
