helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A4				0	ta	Oracle Database Connection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A8				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the options to access an Oracle database.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BD				0	ta	Oracle database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ta	You can use a JDBC driver to access an Oracle database from Solaris or Linux. To access the database from Windows, you need an ODBC driver.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D4				0	ta	On UNIX, ensure that the Oracle database client is installed with JDBC support. The JDBC driver class for the Solaris Oracle client version 8.x is located in the <Oracle client>/product/jdbc/lib/classes111.zip directory. You can also download the latest version of the driver from the Oracle web site:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D7				0	ta	http://otn.oracle.com/tech/java/sqlj_jdbc/content.html				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> box, enter the location of the Oracle database server. The syntax of the URL depends on the database type. See the documentation that came with the JDBC driver for more information.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F1				0	ta	For an Oracle database, the syntax of the URL is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F4				0	ta	oracle:thin:@hostname:port:database_name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FD				0	ta	hostname is the name of the machine that runs the Oracle database. You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10601				0	ta	port is the port where the Oracle database listens. Ask your database administrator for the correct port address.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02oracle.xhp	0	help	par_idN10605				0	ta	database_name is the name of the Oracle database. Ask your database administrator for the correct name.				20200411 15:09:53
