helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153816				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>font sizes; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sizes; of fonts in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	ta	Font Sizes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ta	\<variable id=\"schriftgroessentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONTSIZE\"\>Use this dialog to specify the font sizes for your formula. Select a base size and all elements of the formula will be scaled in relation to this base.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	ta	Base size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:METRICFIELD:RID_FONTSIZEDIALOG:1\"\>All elements of a formula are proportionally scaled to the base size. To change the base size, select or type in the desired point (pt) size. You can also use other units of measure or other \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#metrik\" name=\"metrics\"\>metrics\</link\>, which are then automatically converted to points.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153005				0	ta	To permanently change the default size (12 pt) used in $[officename] Math, you must first set the size (for example, 11 pt) and then click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153735				0	ta	Relative Sizes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ta	In this section, you can determine the relative sizes for each type of element with reference to the base size.				20200411 15:09:53
