helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147546				0	ta	You can also assign an index or an exponent to a function. For example, typing \<emph\>sin^2x\</emph\> results in in a function "sine to the power of 2x".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154752				0	ta	When typing functions manually in the Commands window, note that spaces are required for some functions (for example, abs 5=5 ; abs -3=3).				20200411 15:09:53
