helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156261				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>fonts; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula fonts; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; formula fonts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156261				0	ta	Fonts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	ta	\<variable id=\"schriftartentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONT\"\>Defines the fonts that can be applied to formula elements.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154639				0	ta	Formula Fonts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	ta	You can define fonts for the variables, functions, numbers and inserted text that form the elements of your formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156318				0	ta	The list boxes in the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog display a default font for all elements. To change to a different font, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>, then select the element type. A new dialog box appears. Select the desired font and check any desired attributes, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. To set the changes as the default fonts, click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831				0	ta	If you want to mark individual text segments with a font other than that used for the whole text, then enter the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"FONT\"\>Font\</link\> command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	ta	Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG_1\"\>You can select the fonts for the variables in your formula.\</ahelp\> For example, in the formula x=SIN(y), x and y are variables, and will reflect the assigned font.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150708				0	ta	Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Select the fonts for names and properties of functions.\</ahelp\> For example, the functions in the formula x=SIN(y) are =SIN( ).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149805				0	ta	Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:3\"\>You can select the fonts for the numbers in your formula.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153529				0	ta	Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153780				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:4\"\>Define the fonts for the text in your formula here.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152963				0	ta	Custom Fonts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154566				0	ta	In this section of the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog you can define fonts, with which you can format other text components in the formula. The three basic fonts \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> and \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> are available. You can add any other font to each standard installed basic font. Every font installed on your system is available for you to use. Select the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to expand the selection offered in the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315	17			0	ta	These custom fonts are used if you set a different font with the FONT command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153670				0	ta	Serif				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151108				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:5\"\>You can specify the font to be used for the \<emph\>font serif\</emph\> format.\</ahelp\> Serifs are the small "guides" that can be seen, for example, at the bottom of a capital A when the Times serif font is used. Using serifs is quite helpful since it guides a reader's eye in a straight line and can speed up reading.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150836				0	ta	Sans				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:6\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>sans\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149340				0	ta	Fixed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154198				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:7\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>fixed\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159194				0	ta	Modify				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146932				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:MENUBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:1\"\>Click one of the choices from this pop-up menu to access the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\> dialog, where you can define the font and attributes for the respective formula and for custom fonts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149304				0	ta	Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:PUSHBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Click this button to save your changes as the default for all new formulas.\</ahelp\> After confirming the changes, click the \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Matrix in Bold Font				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090906.xhp\" name=\"Matrix in Bold Font\"\>Matrix in Bold Font\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ta	Here is an example of how to create a bold font matrix in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb6.png\" width=\"9.511cm\" height=\"7.99cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	ta	bold { f(x", "y) = left [ stack { x + y over z + left lbrace matrix { 2 # 3 # 4 ## 4 # 5 # 6 ## 6 # 7 # 8} right rbrace # {y + sin (x)} over %alpha # z + y over g } right ]}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148839				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>attributes; additional information\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148839				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091300.xhp\" name=\"Attributes\"\>Attributes\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ta	Additional information about attributes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> is found here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966				0	ta	The \<emph\>acute\</emph\>, \<emph\>bar\</emph\>, \<emph\>breve\</emph\>, \<emph\>check\</emph\>, \<emph\>circle\</emph\>, \<emph\>dot\</emph\>, \<emph\>ddot\</emph\>, \<emph\>dddot\</emph\>, \<emph\>grave\</emph\>, \<emph\>hat\</emph\>, \<emph\>tilde\</emph\> and \<emph\>vec\</emph\> attributes always have a fixed size and do not become wider (longer) if they are above a long symbol. By default, the attributes are centered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154557				0	ta	The only attributes which grow with the length of the symbol are \<emph\>overline\</emph\>, \<emph\>underline\</emph\> and \<emph\>overstrike\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	ta	For some character strings, it is possible that a line inserted with \<emph\>underline\</emph\> is too close to the character. In this case, an empty group can solve the problem: \<emph\>underline Q sub {}\</emph\> instead of \<emph\>underline Q\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	AutoUpdate Display				20200411 15:09:53
