helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Data Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Data Point\"\>Data Point\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ta	This dialog allows you to change the properties of a selected data point. The dialog appears when there is only one data point selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	ta	Any changes made only affect this one data point. For example, if you edit the color of a bar, only the color of that bar will be different.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	3D View 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>3D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; 3D views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Illumination; 3D charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3464461				0	ta	\<variable id=\"three_d_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ta	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> or in the context menu of a chart you can choose a chart type. \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to edit the properties of a three dimensional view for Column, Bar, Pie, and Area charts. For Line and XY (Scatter) charts you can see 3D lines.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	ta	The chart preview responds to the new settings that you enter in the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ta	When you leave the dialog with OK, the settings are applied permanently. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ta	When you leave the dialog with Cancel or Escape, the chart returns to the state when you opened the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8081911				0	ta	For a 3D chart you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - 3D View\</item\> to set perspective, appearance and illumination.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id2924283				0	ta	Perspective				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	ta	Enter the values for rotation of the chart on the three axes and for a perspective view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9999694				0	ta	Set all angles to 0 for a front view of the chart. Pie charts and donut charts are shown as circles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	ta	With Right-angled axes enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ta	An x value of 90, with y and z set to 0, provides a view from top down to the chart. With x set to -90, you see the bottom of the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ta	The rotations are applied in the order first x, then y, last z.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ta	When shading is enabled and you rotate a chart, the lights are rotated as if they are fixed to the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2578203				0	ta	The rotation axes always relate to the page, not to the chart's axes. This is different from some other chart programs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4923245				0	ta	Select the Perspective check box to view the chart in central perspective as through a camera lens instead of using a parallel projection. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3416547				0	ta	Set the focus length with the spin button. 100% gives a perspective view where a far edge in the chart looks approximately half as big as a near edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ta	Older versions of %PRODUCTNAME cannot display the percentage of perspective the same way as the current version.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Right-angled axes is enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders. Right-angled axes is enabled by default for newly created 3D charts. Pie and Donut charts do not support right-angled axes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the x axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the y axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the z axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark the Perspective box to view the chart as through a camera lens. Use the spin button to set the percentage. With a high percentage nearer objects look bigger than more distant objects.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id7564012				0	ta	Appearance				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	ta	Select a scheme from the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	ta	By selecting a scheme, the check boxes and the light sources are set accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	ta	If you mark or unmark a combination of check boxes that is not given by the Realistic or Simple scheme, you create a Custom scheme.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1579027				0	ta	Mark \<emph\>Shading\</emph\> to use the Gouraud method for rendering the surface, otherwise a flat method is used. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5624561				0	ta	The flat method sets a single color and brightness for each polygon. The edges are visible, soft gradients and spot lights are not possible. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5901058				0	ta	The Gouraud method applies gradients for a smoother, more realistic look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8469191				0	ta	Mark \<emph\>Object Borders\</emph\> to draw lines along the edges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4407483				0	ta	Mark \<emph\>Rounded Edges\</emph\> to smooth the edges of box shapes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a scheme from the list box, or click any of the check boxes below.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies Gouraud shading if marked, or flat shading if unmarked.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows borders around the areas by setting the line style to Solid.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edges are rounded by 5%.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id1939451				0	ta	Illumination				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	ta	Set the light sources for the 3D view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	ta	Click any of the eight buttons to switch a directed light source on or off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	ta	By default, the second light source is switched on. It is the first of seven "normal", uniform light sources. The light source number one projects a specular light with highlights.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ta	For the selected light source, you can then choose a color and intensity in the list box just below the eight buttons. The brightness values of all lights are added, so use dark colors when you enable multiple lights.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ta	The small preview inside this tab page has two sliders to set the vertical and horizontal position of the selected light source. The light source always aims to the middle of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ta	The button in the corner of the small preview switches the internal illumination model between a sphere and a cube.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ta	Use the Ambient light list box to define the ambient light which shines with a uniform intensity from all directions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the right slider to set the vertical height and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the bottom slider to set the horizontal position and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to switch between an illumination model of a sphere or a cube.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the specular light source with highlights.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the uniform light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color for the ambient light.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a color using the color dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Titles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147345				0	ta	Titles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	ta	\<variable id=\"titel\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMenuTitles\"\>Opens a dialog to enter or modify the titles in a chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can define the text for the main title, subtitle and the axis labels, and specify if they are displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ta	Main Title				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150371				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_MAINTITLE\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Main Title\</emph\> option activates the main title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146980				0	ta	Subtitle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_SUBTITLE\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Subtitle\</emph\> option activates the subtitle. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sytexttitel\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleTitle\"\>Click \<emph\>Title On/Off\</emph\> on the Formatting bar to show or hide the title and subtitle.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156018				0	ta	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_X_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>X axis\</emph\> option activates the X axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159226				0	ta	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_Y_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Y axis\</emph\> option activates the Y axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153009				0	ta	Z axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154710				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:EDIT:DLG_TITLE:EDT_Z_AXIS\"\>Marking the \<emph\>Z axis\</emph\> option activates the Z axis title. Enter the desired title in the corresponding text field.\</ahelp\> This option is only available for 3-D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sytextachse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisTitle\"\>Click \<emph\>Axes Title On/Off\</emph\> on the Formatting bar to show or hide the axis labels.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Axes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147428				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>axes; showing axes in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; showing axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Z axes; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes; better scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>secondary axes in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	ta	Axes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	ta	\<variable id=\"achsen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMenuAxes\"\>Specifies the axes to be displayed in the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	ta	Major axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146316				0	ta	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_CHECKBOX_DLG_AXIS_CB_X_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the X axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147003				0	ta	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the Y axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	ta	Z axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Z_PRIMARY\"\>Displays the Z axis as a line with subdivisions.\</ahelp\> This axis can only be displayed in 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	ta	Secondary axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	ta	Use this area to assign a second axis to your chart. If a data series is already assigned to this axis, $[officename] automatically displays the axis and the label. You can turn off these settings later on. If no data has been assigned to this axis and you activate this area, the values of the primary Y axis are applied to the secondary axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152988				0	ta	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_X_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary X axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152896				0	ta	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary Y axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Y Error Bars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	ta	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	ta	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	ta	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	ta	Error category				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Error category\</emph\> area, you can choose different ways to display the error category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152989				0	ta	None				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_NONE\"\>Does not show any error bars.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145117				0	ta	Constant value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_MINUS\"\>Displays constant values that you specify in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159204				0	ta	Percentage				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150048				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_PERCENT\"\>Displays a percentage. The display refers to the corresponding data point. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id8977629				0	ta	Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id7109286				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select a function to calculate the error bars.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5154576				0	ta	Standard Error: Displays the standard error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Variance: Displays the variance calculated from the number of data points and respective values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Standard Deviation: Displays the standard deviation (square root of the variance).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Error Margin: Displays the highest error margin in percent according to the highest value of the data group. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id350962				0	ta	Cell Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6679586				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3872188				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2633747				0	ta	From Data Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6633503				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a chart with its own data, the error bar values can be entered in the chart data table. The Data Table dialog shows additional columns titled Positive Y-Error-Bars and Negative Y-Error-Bars.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573839				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
