helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143219				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040100.xhp\" name=\"X Axis\"\>X Axis\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Y Axis\"\>Y Axis\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05050100.xhp\" name=\"Grid\"\>Grid\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Chart Floor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>charts; formatting floors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart floors\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	ta	Chart Floor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	2			0	ta	\<variable id=\"diagrammboden\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramFloor\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Chart Floor\</emph\> dialog, where you can modify the properties of the chart floor. The chart floor is the lower area in 3D charts. This function is only available for 3D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Chart Wizard - Data Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id8641621				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>order of chart data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id6124149				0	ta	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Series\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9651478				0	ta	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can change the source range of all data series separately, including their labels. You can also change the range of the categories. You can first select the data range on the Data Range page and then remove unnecessary data series or add data series from other cells here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6326487				0	ta	If there seem to be too many options on this page, just define the data range on the Chart Wizard - Data Range page and skip this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id686361				0	ta	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9241615				0	ta	Organizing data series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7159337				0	ta	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4921720				0	ta	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6627094				0	ta	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	ta	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4443800				0	ta	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9777520				0	ta	Editing data series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1474654				0	ta	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4855189				0	ta	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9475081				0	ta	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4695272				0	ta	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3931699				0	ta	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	ta	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5971556				0	ta	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id7622608				0	ta	Editing categories or data labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9222693				0	ta	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9500106				0	ta	Depending on the chart type, the texts are shown on the X axis or as data labels. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address of the categories (the texts you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an XY-chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1091647				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds a new entry below the current entry in the Data Series list. If an entry is selected, the new data series gets the same chart type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8831446				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7022309				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves up the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2844019				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves down the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>axes; inserting grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; inserting in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	ta	Grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ta	\<variable id=\"gitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can divide the axes into sections by assigning gridlines to them. This allows you to get a better overview of the chart, especially if you are working with large charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The Y axis major grid is activated by default.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156286				0	ta	Major grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511				0	ta	Defines the axis to be set as the major grid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	ta	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the X axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sytextxgitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridHorizontal\"\>The \<emph\>Horizontal Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the X axis. Note: This only works if the \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> check boxes in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\> are cleared.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	ta	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Y axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sytextygitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridVertical\"\>The \<emph\>Vertical Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the Y axis. Note: This only works if the X-axis \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> is not selected in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166430				0	ta	Z axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Z axis of the chart.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146978				0	ta	Minor grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156449				0	ta	Use this area to assign a minor grid for each axis. Assigning minor grids to the axis reduces the distance between the major grids.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153308				0	ta	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148704				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the X axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153917				0	ta	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154536				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Y axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148607				0	ta	Z axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153247				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Z axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Chart Wizard - Chart Elements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id70802				0	ta	\<variable id=\"wiz_chart_elements\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_elements.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Chart Elements\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id8746604				0	ta	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose the chart elements to be shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6437269				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a title for your chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9469893				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a subtitle for your chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id130008				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the x-axis (horizontal).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the y-axis (vertical).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2871791				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays a legend in your chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the left of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the top of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the right of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Positions the legend to the bottom of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6917020				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9969481				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the secondary x-axis. This option is only available for charts that support a secondary x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id816675				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a label for the secondary y-axis. This option is only available for charts that support a secondary y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id4411145				0	ta	To enter chart elements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id3274941				0	ta	Enter titles or click the elements that you want to be shown on the current chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	hd_id9804681				0	ta	Titles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id3614917				0	ta	If you enter text for a title, subtitle, or any axis, the necessary space will be reserved to display the text next to the chart. If you do not enter a text, no space will be reserved, leaving more space to display the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id156865				0	ta	It is not possible to link the title text to a cell. You must enter the text directly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6034424				0	ta	When the chart is finished, you can change the position and other properties by the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	ta	Legend				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	ta	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column, or from the range that you have set in the Data Series dialog. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ta	You cannot enter the text directly, it is automatically generated from the Name cell range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id71413				0	ta	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id4776757				0	ta	Grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6737876				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the x-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id1058992				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the y-axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id7366557				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays grid lines that are perpendicular to the z-axis. This option is only available for three-dimensional charts.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	ta	The visible grid lines can help to estimate the data values in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	ta	The distance of the grid lines corresponds to the interval settings in the Scale tab of the axis properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_elements.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	ta	Grid lines are not available for pie charts.				20200411 15:09:53
