helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	About Layers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ta	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	ta	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	ta	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	ta	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	ta	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	ta	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	ta	Layout				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	ta	Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ta	Dimension Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	ta	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	ta	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	ta	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	ta	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	ta	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>importing; presentations with HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; importing HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing into presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; text in presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	ta	\<variable id=\"html_import\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_import.xhp\" name=\"Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \"\>Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	ta	You can import any text file, including text in HTML documents, into a slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	ta	To insert text from a file into a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	ta	In the slide where you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150207				0	ta	Select "Text" or "HTML Document" as the \<emph\>File type\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	ta	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	ta	If the text file contains more text than can be inserted into a single slide, you can divide the text over several slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ta	Double-click in the inserted text to enter edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	ta	Select all of the text that lies below the visible slide area and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert – Slide\</emph\>, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3147297				0	ta	Repeat steps 1 to 3 until all of the text is on slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Saving a Presentation in HTML Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155067				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;presentations to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; exporting to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; exporting from presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	ta	\<variable id=\"html_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_export.xhp\" name=\"Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\"\>Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	ta	Open the presentation that you want to save in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3149502				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842				0	ta	Set the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> to \<emph\>HTML Document ($[officename] Impress) (.html;.htm)\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	ta	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153808				0	ta	Follow the instructions in the \<emph\>HTML Export\</emph\> Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01110000.xhp\" name=\"HTML Export AutoPilot\"\>HTML Export Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3150394				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/01170000.xhp\" name=\"File - Export\"\>File - Export\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>slide designs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; designing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master pages, see slide masters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ta	\<variable id=\"masterpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/masterpage.xhp\" name=\"Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\"\>Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ta	Every slide in a presentation has exactly one slide master, also known as master page. A slide master determines the text formatting style for the title and outline and the background design for all slides that use this slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ta	To apply a new slide master				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ta	Select \<emph\>Format - Slide Design\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ta	Under \<emph\>Categories\</emph\>, select a slide design category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	26			0	ta	Under \<emph\>Templates\</emph\>, select a template with the design that you want to apply. To preview the template, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Preview \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	ta	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	ta	To apply the slide design to all of the slides in your presentation, select the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	ta	To apply the slide design to the current slide only, clear the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Including Spreadsheets in Slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154022				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>including spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	ta	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Including Spreadsheets in Slides\"\>Including Spreadsheets in Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	ta	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	ta	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	ta	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centered in the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Selects the current table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	ta	Inserting a native table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	ta	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	ta	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	ta	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	ta	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	ta	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	ta	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	ta	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	ta	Inserting a new spreadsheet as an OLE object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	ta	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ta	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	ta	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	ta	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	ta	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765				0	ta	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112				0	ta	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ta	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	ta	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	ta	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256				0	ta	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
