helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ta	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	ta	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ta	To create a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	ta	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	ta	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	ta	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging and dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	ta	To start a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	ta	Select the show you want to start from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	ta	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169				0	ta	Options for Running a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335				0	ta	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	ta	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153922				0	ta	To hide a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id883150344				0	ta	To hide the current slide, click the Hide Slide action button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	ta	To hide several slides, choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the slide(s) that you want to hide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3083278				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	ta	The slide is not removed from your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147570				0	ta	To show a hidden slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145210				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the hidden slide(s) that you want to show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153191				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>footers;slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers and footers; slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;headers/footers in all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time and date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	ta	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	ta	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	ta	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	ta	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	ta	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	ta	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	ta	Adding predefined header or footer objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	ta	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	ta	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	ta	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	ta	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	ta	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	ta	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	ta	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	ta	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	ta	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	ta	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	ta	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	ta	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id4712057				0	ta	Adding text objects as header or footer objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	ta	You can add a text object anywhere on the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	ta	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ta	Drag in the slide master to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155441				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> when you are finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	ta	You can also add fields, such as the date or page number, to a header or footer by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	18			0	ta	You can hide the header or footer on the current slide by choosing \<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Modify Layout\"\>Slide\<emph\> Layout\</emph\>\</link\>, and clearing the \<emph\>Objects on background\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
