helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ta	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	ta	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	ta	To create an animated GIF:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	ta	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	ta	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	ta	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	ta	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	ta	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	ta	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	ta	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	ta	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	ta	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	ta	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ta	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ta	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ta	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	ta	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ta	3D object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	ta	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	ta	Two types of 3D objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	ta	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	ta	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	ta	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ta	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	ta	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	ta	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	ta	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ta	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ta	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	ta	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	ta	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	ta	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	ta	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	ta	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	ta	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	ta	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	ta	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	ta	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	ta	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	ta	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Selecting Underlying Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	ta	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	ta	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ta	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Drawing Curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149377				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>control points definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>corner points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing;lines\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	ta	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Drawing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	ta	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar opens a toolbar to draw Bézier curves. Bézier curves are defined by a start point and an end point, which are called "anchors". The curvature of the Bézier curve is defined by control points ("handles"). Moving a control point changes the shape of the Bézier curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8532364				0	ta	Control points are only visible in "Edit Points" mode. Control points are represented by circles, anchor points are represented by squares. The start point is a little bit larger than the other anchor points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ta	Bézier curve segments and straight line segments can be joined to form more complex Bézier curves. Three different transitions can be applied to join adjacent segments:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	ta	A \<emph\>symmetrical\</emph\> anchor point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	ta	A \<emph\>smooth\</emph\> anchor point may have different line curvatures on either side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435				0	ta	A \<emph\>corner\</emph\> anchor point has one or two independent control lines. Changing one side has no effect on the other side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	ta	How to use the Curve tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	ta	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic1\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	ta	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag in the direction where you want the curve to go. The control line will indicate the direction. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8174687				0	ta	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag to restrict the direction to a 45 degree grid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	ta	Release the mouse where the first control point should be.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	ta	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end. The curve follows the pointer. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	ta	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	ta	Double-click on the position of the end point to finish drawing the line. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	ta	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	ta	Click and release the mouse button to add an anchor point. Move the mouse to draw the next segment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451				0	ta	Click and drag in any direction to add a smooth anchor point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id2071596				0	ta	How to use the Freeform Line tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	ta	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	ta	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	ta	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id7734916				0	ta	Release the mouse button to finish the line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Printing Presentations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>printing; presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>slides; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>notes; printing in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>outlines; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>presentations; printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tiled printing of slides\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;layout for handouts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handout printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>layout;printing handouts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	ta	\<variable id=\"printing\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/printing.xhp\" name=\"Printing Presentations\"\>Printing Presentations\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	ta	Default printer settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	ta	To set the default printing options for $[officename] Impress, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153914				0	ta	Setting printer options for the current presentation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, and then select the printer options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	ta	These settings override the default printer options in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\> for the current print job only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id4555192				0	ta	Choosing a print layout for handouts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id7197790				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1104159				0	ta	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, select the "Handouts" entry from the Document listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id9354533				0	ta	Select the number of slides to print per page of paper.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id6556596				0	ta	Defining print options for handouts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6744285				0	ta	Click the Handout tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id996734				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Page Number\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Header and Footer\</emph\> dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6752220				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> to enter the header and footer text for handouts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5703909				0	ta	You see four areas on this dialog with check boxes for Header, Date and time, Footer, and Page number. These four areas correspond to the four areas in the corners of the handout master view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id4984282				0	ta	Enter text for header, footer, and date. Check the \<emph\>Page number\</emph\> box, if you want to number the handout pages. Ensure the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> check box is enabled if you want your header text to be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
