helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149499				0	ta	\<variable id=\"arrange_slides\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/arrange_slides.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Order\"\>Changing the Slide Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	ta	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, select one or more slides, and then drag the slides to another location. To select multiple slides, hold down shift and click on the slides. To create a copy of a selected slide, hold down Ctrl while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to a plus sign. You can also drag a copy of a slide into another open $[officename] Impress document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153072				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Outline\</emph\>, select a slide, and then drag the slide to another location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\>, select the slide preview on the \<emph\>Slides Pane\</emph\>, and then drag the slide preview to another location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153079				0	ta	To temporarily remove a slide from your presentation, go to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\>, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>. The number of the hidden slide is crossed out. To show the slide, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size				20200411 15:09:53
