helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	ta	\<variable id=\"print_tofit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/print_tofit.xhp\" name=\"Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\"\>Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	ta	You can reduce the size of a slide when you print, so that the slide can fit on a printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	ta	Open the document that you want to print.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ta	In \<emph\>Normal View\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	6			0	ta	In \<emph\>Layout settings \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Fit object to paper format\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\> area, select a \<emph\>Format\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The slide is resized to fit the printed page, while maintaining the relative positions of the objects on the slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				20200411 15:09:53
