helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153718				0	ta	Animations allowed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3083445				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:CHECKBOX:DLG_START_PRESENTATION:CBX_ANIMATION_ALLOWED\"\>Displays all frames of animated GIF files during the slide show.\</ahelp\> If this option is not selected, only the first frame of an animated GIF file is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152478				0	ta	Change slides by clicking on background				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156305				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:CHECKBOX:DLG_START_PRESENTATION:CBX_CHANGE_PAGE\"\>Advances to the next slide when you click on the background of a slide.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150960				0	ta	Presentation always on top				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:CHECKBOX:DLG_START_PRESENTATION:CBX_ALWAYS_ON_TOP\"\>The $[officename] window remains on top during the presentation. No other program will show its window in front of your presentation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id6086611				0	ta	Multiple Monitors				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id5446943				0	ta	By default the primary monitor is used for slide show mode. If the current desktop is displayed on more than one monitor, you can select which monitor to use for full screen slide show mode. If the current desktop spans only one monitor, or if the multi monitor feature is not supported on the current system, you cannot select another monitor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id4962309				0	ta	Presentation Monitor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id5168919				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select a monitor to use for full screen slide show mode.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id4846339				0	ta	If the system allows to span a window over all available monitors, you can also select "All monitors". In this case the presentation spans over all available monitors. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id2321543				0	ta	This setting is saved in the user configuration and not inside the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	To Contour 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>converting; to contours\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contours; converting to\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050700.xhp\" name=\"To Contour\"\>To Contour\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:convert_to_contour\"\>Converts the selected object to a polygon, or a group of polygons.\</ahelp\> If the conversion creates a group of polygons (for example, when you convert a text object), then press F3 to enter the group before you can select an individual polygon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	3			0	ta	Once you convert a line or a text object to a contour, you can no longer edit it as you normally would. Instead, you can edit the contour as you would any polygon, including using the \<emph\>Edit – Points \</emph\>command to adjust its shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Outline				20200411 15:09:53
