helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145208				0	ta	13				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	78			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>>0\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153625	79			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>Total\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151297	80			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>40,000.00 currency units\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149979				0	ta	The formula in E2 is as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155849	82			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SYD($A$2;$B$2;$C$2;D2)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156124				0	ta	This formula is duplicated in column E down to E11 (select E2, then drag down the lower right corner with the mouse).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147270				0	ta	Cell E13 contains the formula used to check the total of the depreciation amounts. It uses the SUMIF function as the negative values in E8:E11 must not be considered. The condition >0 is contained in cell A13. The formula in E13 is as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	85			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(E2:E11;A13)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155998				0	ta	Now view the depreciation for a 10 year period, or at a salvage value of 1 currency unit, or enter a different initial cost, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155104				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>DISC function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>allowances\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>discounts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155104				0	ta	DISC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_DISC\"\>Calculates the allowance (discount) of a security as a percentage.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153982				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	ta	DISC("Settlement"; "Maturity"; Price; Redemption; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156014	383			0	ta	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	384			0	ta	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180	385			0	ta	            \<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253	386			0	ta	            \<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151174				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the maturity date is 2001-11-15. The price (purchase price) is 97, the redemption value is 100. Using daily balance calculation (basis 3) how high is the settlement (discount)?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152797	389			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DISC("2001-01-25";"2001-11-15";97;100;3)\</item\> returns about 0.0372 or 3.72 per cent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154695				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>DURATION_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Excel functions\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>durations;fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154695				0	ta	DURATION_ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145768				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_DURATION\"\>Calculates the duration of a fixed interest security in years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153904				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153373				0	ta	DURATION_ADD("Settlement"; "Maturity"; Coupon; Yield; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155397	406			0	ta	            \<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148558	407			0	ta	            \<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153096	408			0	ta	            \<emph\>Coupon\</emph\> is the annual coupon interest rate (nominal rate of interest)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154594	409			0	ta	            \<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906	410			0	ta	            \<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146995				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148834				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-01; the maturity date is 2006-01-01. The Coupon rate of interest is 8%. The yield is 9.0%. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how long is the duration?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154902	413			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DURATION_ADD("2001-01-01";"2006-01-01";0.08;0.09;2;3)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159147				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>net annual interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECTIVE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159147				0	ta	EFFECTIVE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154204				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EFFEKTIV\"\>Returns the net annual interest rate for a nominal interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417				0	ta	Nominal interest refers to the amount of interest due at the end of a calculation period. Effective interest increases with the number of payments made. In other words, interest is often paid in installments (for example, monthly or quarterly) before the end of the calculation period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150510				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148805				0	ta	EFFECTIVE(Nom; P)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768	93			0	ta	            \<emph\>Nom\</emph\> is the nominal interest.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149334	94			0	ta	            \<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of interest payment periods per year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154223				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144499				0	ta	If the annual nominal interest rate is 9.75% and four interest calculation periods are defined, what is the actual interest rate (effective rate)?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	97			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECTIVE(9.75%;4)\</item\> = 10.11% The annual effective rate is therefore 10.11%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147241				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>effective interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147241				0	ta	EFFECT_ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_EFFECT\"\>Calculates the effective annual rate of interest on the basis of the nominal interest rate and the number of interest payments per annum.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155118				0	ta	EFFECT_ADD(NominalRate; NPerY)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148907	418			0	ta	            \<emph\>NominalRate\</emph\> is the annual nominal rate of interest.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154274	419			0	ta	            \<emph\>NPerY \</emph\>is the number of interest payments per year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149156				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3158426				0	ta	What is the effective annual rate of interest for a 5.25% nominal rate and quarterly payment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148927	422			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECT_ADD(0.0525;4)\</item\> returns 0.053543 or 5.3543%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149998				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>arithmetic-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;arithmetic-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DDB function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149998				0	ta	DDB				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159190				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the arithmetic-declining method.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	ta	Use this form of depreciation if you require a higher initial depreciation value as opposed to linear depreciation. The depreciation value gets less with each period and is usually used for assets whose value loss is higher shortly after purchase (for example, vehicles, computers). Please note that the book value will never reach zero under this calculation type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156038				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3166452				0	ta	DDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Factor)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153237	104			0	ta	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> fixes the initial cost of an asset.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149787	105			0	ta	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> fixes the value of an asset at the end of its life.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	106			0	ta	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the number of periods (for example, years or months) defining how long the asset is to be used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149736	107			0	ta	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> states the period for which the value is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150243	108			0	ta	            \<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the factor by which depreciation decreases. If a value is not entered, the default is factor 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159274				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152882				0	ta	A computer system with an initial cost of 75,000 currency units is to be depreciated monthly over 5 years. The value at the end of the depreciation is to be 1 currency unit. The factor is 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154106	111			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DDB(75000;1;60;12;2) \</item\>= 1,721.81 currency units. Therefore, the double-declining depreciation in the twelfth month after purchase is 1,721.81 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149962				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>geometric-degressive depreciations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>depreciations;geometric-degressive\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>DB function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149962				0	ta	DB				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148989				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GDA2\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified period using the double-declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156213				0	ta	This form of depreciation is used if you want to get a higher depreciation value at the beginning of the depreciation (as opposed to linear depreciation). The depreciation value is reduced with every depreciation period by the depreciation already deducted from the initial cost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149807				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	ta	DB(Cost; Salvage; Life; Period; Month)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148462	118			0	ta	            \<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial cost of an asset.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148658	119			0	ta	            \<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145371	120			0	ta	            \<emph\>Life\</emph\> defines the period over which an asset is depreciated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154608	121			0	ta	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the length of each period. The length must be entered in the same date unit as the depreciation period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150829	122			0	ta	            \<emph\>Month\</emph\> (optional) denotes the number of months for the first year of depreciation. If an entry is not defined, 12 is used as the default.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151130				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156147				0	ta	A computer system with an initial cost of 25,000 currency units is to be depreciated over a three year period. The salvage value is to be 1,000 currency units. One period is 30 days.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149513	125			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DB(25000;1000;36;1;6)\</item\> = 1,075.00 currency units				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159242				0	ta	The fixed-declining depreciation of the computer system is 1,075.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153948				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>IRR function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, regular payments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;regular payments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153948				0	ta	IRR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_IKV\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for an investment.\</ahelp\> The values represent cash flow values at regular intervals, at least one value must be negative (payments), and at least one value must be positive (income).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150599				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155427				0	ta	IRR(Values; Guess)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144758	132			0	ta	            \<emph\>Values\</emph\> represents an array containing the values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	133			0	ta	            \<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) is the estimated value. An iterative method is used to calculate the internal rate of return. If you can provide only few values, you should provide an initial guess to enable the iteration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151258				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630				0	ta	Under the assumption that cell contents are A1=\<item type=\"input\"\>-10000\</item\>, A2=\<item type=\"input\"\>3500\</item\>, A3=\<item type=\"input\"\>7600\</item\> and A4=\<item type=\"input\"\>1000\</item\>, the formula \<item type=\"input\"\>=IRR(A1:A4)\</item\> gives a result of 11,33%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151012				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>interests for unchanged amortization installments\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>ISPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151012				0	ta	ISPMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148693				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ISPMT\"\>Calculates the level of interest for unchanged amortization installments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146070				0	ta	ISPMT(Rate; Period; TotalPeriods; Invest)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	318			0	ta	            \<emph\>Rate\</emph\> sets the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777	319			0	ta	            \<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the number of installments for calculation of interest.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678	320			0	ta	            \<emph\>TotalPeriods\</emph\> is the total number of installment periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390	321			0	ta	            \<emph\>Invest\</emph\> is the amount of the investment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156162				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149558				0	ta	For a credit amount of 120,000 currency units with a two-year term and monthly installments, at a yearly interest rate of 12% the level of interest after 1.5 years is required.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949	324			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=ISPMT(1%;18;24;120000)\</item\> = -300 currency units. The monthly interest after 1.5 years amounts to 300 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146812				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060119.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Two\"\>Financial Functions Part Two\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\"\>Financial Functions Part Three\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Define Names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156330				0	ta	Define Names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ta	\<variable id=\"namenfestlegentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefineName\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify a name for a selected area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	31			0	ta	Use the mouse to define ranges or type the reference into the \<emph\>Define Name \</emph\>dialog fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	ta	The \<emph\>Sheet Area\</emph\> box on the Formula bar contains a list of defined names for the ranges. Click a name from this box to highlight the corresponding reference on the spreadsheet. Names given formulas or parts of a formula are not listed here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151118				0	ta	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:COMBOBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:ED_NAME\"\>Enter the name of the area for which you want to define a reference. All area names already defined in the spreadsheet are listed in the text field below.\</ahelp\> If you click a name on the list, the corresponding reference in the document will be shown with a blue frame. If multiple cell ranges belong to the same area name, they are displayed with different colored frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	ta	Assigned to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:ED_ASSIGN\"\>The reference of the selected area name is shown here as an absolute value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	ta	To insert a new area reference, place the cursor in this field and use your mouse to select the desired area in any sheet of your spreadsheet document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	ta	More				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	14			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MOREBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_MORE\"\>Allows you to specify the \<emph\>Area type \</emph\>(optional) for the reference.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147394				0	ta	Area type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155416				0	ta	Defines additional options related to the type of reference area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	ta	Print range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_PRINTAREA\"\>Defines the area as a print range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	ta	Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_CRITERIA\"\>Defines the selected area to be used in an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040300.xhp\" name=\"advanced filter\"\>advanced filter\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159267				0	ta	Repeat column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_COLHEADER\"\>Defines the area as a repeating column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	ta	Repeat row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150300				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_ROWHEADER\"\>Defines the area as a repeating row.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155112				0	ta	Add/Modify				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:BTN_ADD\"\>Click the \<emph\>Add\</emph\> button to add the defined name to the list. Click the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to enter another name for an already existing name selected from the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Statistical Functions Part One				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146320				0	ta	\<variable id=\"ae\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060181.xhp\"\>Statistical Functions Part One\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145632				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>INTERCEPT function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>points of intersection\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>intersections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145632				0	ta	INTERCEPT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146887				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ACHSENABSCHNITT\"\>Calculates the point at which a line will intersect the y-values by using known x-values and y-values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150374				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149718				0	ta	INTERCEPT(DataY; DataX)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947	6			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataY\</emph\> is the dependent set of observations or data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412	7			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataX\</emph\> is the independent set of observations or data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152983				0	ta	Names, arrays or references containing numbers must be used here. Numbers can also be entered directly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157906				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	ta	To calculate the intercept, use cells D3:D9 as the y value and C3:C9 as the x value from the example spreadsheet. Input will be as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149013	11			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=INTERCEPT(D3:D9;C3:C9)\</item\> = 2.15.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148437				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUNT function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>numbers;counting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148437				0	ta	COUNT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL\"\>Counts how many numbers are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153930				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148585				0	ta	COUNT(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155827	17			0	ta	            \<emph\>Value1; Value2, ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 values or ranges representing the values to be counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149254				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953				0	ta	The entries 2, 4, 6 and eight in the Value 1-4 fields are to be counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	20			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNT(2;4;6;"eight")\</item\> = 3. The count of numbers is therefore 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149729				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTA function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>number of entries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149729				0	ta	COUNTA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL2\"\>Counts how many values are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are also counted, even when they contain an empty string of length 0. If an argument is an array or reference, empty cells within the array or reference are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148573				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153111				0	ta	COUNTA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001	26			0	ta	            \<emph\>Value1; Value2, ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments representing the values to be counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150334				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154508				0	ta	The entries 2, 4, 6 and eight in the Value 1-4 fields are to be counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158000	29			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTA(2;4;6;"eight")\</item\> = 4. The count of values is therefore 4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150267				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>B function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>probabilities of samples with binomial distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150267				0	ta	B				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_B\"\>Returns the probability of a sample with binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150659				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148392				0	ta	B(Trials; SP; T1; T2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149002	35			0	ta	            \<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148875	36			0	ta	            \<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145352	37			0	ta	            \<emph\>T1\</emph\> defines the lower limit for the number of trials.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149538	38			0	ta	            \<emph\>T2\</emph\> (optional) defines the upper limit for the number of trials.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154633				0	ta	What is the probability with ten throws of the dice, that a six will come up exactly twice? The probability of a six (or any other number) is 1/6. The following formula combines these factors:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149393	41			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=B(10;1/6;2)\</item\> returns a probability of 29%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158416				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>RSQ function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>determination coefficients\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>regression analysis\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158416				0	ta	RSQ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154949				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BESTIMMTHEITSMASS\"\>Returns the square of the Pearson correlation coefficient based on the given values.\</ahelp\> RSQ (also called determination coefficient) is a measure for the accuracy of an adjustment and can be used to produce a regression analysis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152820				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155822				0	ta	RSQ(DataY; DataX)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470	47			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataY\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153181	48			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataX\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156258				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991	50			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=RSQ(A1:A20;B1:B20)\</item\> calculates the determination coefficient for both data sets in columns A and B.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145620				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>BETAINV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>cumulative probability density function;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145620				0	ta	BETAINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BETAINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the cumulative beta probability density function.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152479				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156300				0	ta	BETAINV(Number; Alpha; Beta; Start; End)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149266	56			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value between \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> at which to evaluate the function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149710	57			0	ta	            \<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156306	58			0	ta	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960	59			0	ta	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> (optional) is the lower bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151268	60			0	ta	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the upper bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_idN109DF				0	ta	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147077				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146859	62			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BETAINV(0.5;5;10)\</item\> returns the value 0.33.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156096				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>BETADIST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>cumulative probability density function;calculating\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156096				0	ta	BETADIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150880				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BETAVERT\"\>Returns the beta function.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150762				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ta	BETADIST(Number; Alpha; Beta; Start; End; Cumulative)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	68			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value between \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> at which to evaluate the function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107	69			0	ta	            \<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153619	70			0	ta	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254	71			0	ta	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> (optional) is the lower bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149138	72			0	ta	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the upper bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id012020091254453				0	ta	            \<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional) can be 0 or False to calculate the probability density function. It can be any other value or True or omitted to calculate the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB3				0	ta	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145649				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156118	74			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BETADIST(0.75;3;4)\</item\> returns the value 0.96				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143228				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>BINOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228				0	ta	BINOMDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BINOMVERT\"\>Returns the individual term binomial distribution probability.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149289				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156009				0	ta	BINOMDIST(X; Trials; SP; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	80			0	ta	            \<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of successes in a set of trials.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492	81			0	ta	            \<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146085	82			0	ta	            \<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	83			0	ta	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the probability of a single event and \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the cumulative probability.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145666	85			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;0)\</item\> shows (if the values \<item type=\"input\"\>0\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>12\</item\> are entered in A1) the probabilities for 12 flips of a coin that \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> will come up exactly the number of times entered in A1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150120	86			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;1)\</item\> shows the cumulative probabilities for the same series. For example, if A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>, the cumulative probability of the series is 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4 times \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> (non-exclusive OR).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902432928				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902421451				0	ta	CHISQINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902421449				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the inverse of CHISQDIST.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902475241				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475286				0	ta	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse of the chi-square distribution is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475282				0	ta	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148835				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>CHIINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148835				0	ta	CHIINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the one-tailed probability of the chi-squared distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159157				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	ta	CHIINV(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898	92			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the error probability.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	93			0	ta	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154208				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777				0	ta	A die is thrown 1020 times. The numbers on the die 1 through 6 come up 195, 151, 148, 189, 183 and 154 times (observation values). The hypothesis that the die is not fixed is to be tested.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	ta	The Chi square distribution of the random sample is determined by the formula given above. Since the expected value for a given number on the die for n throws is n times 1/6, thus 1020/6 = 170, the formula returns a Chi square value of 13.27.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148806				0	ta	If the (observed) Chi square is greater than or equal to the (theoretical) Chi square CHIINV, the hypothesis will be discarded, since the deviation between theory and experiment is too great. If the observed Chi square is less that CHIINV, the hypothesis is confirmed with the indicated probability of error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	95			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.05;5)\</item\> returns 11.07.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159142	133			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.02;5)\</item\> returns 13.39.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158401				0	ta	If the probability of error is 5%, the die is not true. If the probability of error is 2%, there is no reason to believe it is fixed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154260				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>CHITEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154260				0	ta	CHITEST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHITEST\"\>Returns the probability of a deviance from a random distribution of two test series based on the chi-squared test for independence.\</ahelp\> CHITEST returns the chi-squared distribution of the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	ta	The probability determined by CHITEST can also be determined with CHIDIST, in which case the Chi square of the random sample must then be passed as a parameter instead of the data row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154280				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149162				0	ta	CHITEST(DataB; DataE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158421	101			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataB\</emph\> is the array of the observations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3166453	102			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataE\</emph\> is the range of the expected values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146946				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	ta	Data_B (observed)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152948				0	ta	Data_E (expected)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876				0	ta	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159279	139			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>195\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149105	140			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149922				0	ta	2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148621	142			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>151\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148987	143			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	ta	3				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148661	145			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>148\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151128	146			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148467				0	ta	4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149237	148			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>189\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145304	149			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149927				0	ta	5				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630	151			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>183\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150423	152			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275				0	ta	6				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3144750	154			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>154\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153947	155			0	ta	                     \<item type=\"input\"\>170\</item\>                  				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	104			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHITEST(A1:A6;B1:B6)\</item\> equals 0.02. This is the probability which suffices the observed data of the theoretical Chi-square distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148690				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>CHIDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148690				0	ta	CHIDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIVERT\"\>Returns the probability value from the indicated Chi square that a hypothesis is confirmed.\</ahelp\> CHIDIST compares the Chi square value to be given for a random sample that is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected value for all values with the theoretical Chi square distribution and determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be tested.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151316				0	ta	The probability determined by CHIDIST can also be determined by CHITEST.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158439				0	ta	CHIDIST(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148675	110			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the chi-square value of the random sample used to determine the error probability.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615	111			0	ta	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> are the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146787				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	113			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIDIST(13.27; 5)\</item\> equals 0.02.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156141				0	ta	If the Chi square value of the random sample is 13.27 and if the experiment has 5 degrees of freedom, then the hypothesis is assured with a probability of error of 2%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902231887				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chi-square distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200901583452				0	ta	CHISQDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200901583471				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the value of the probability density function or the cumulative distribution function for the chi-square distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902395520				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395679				0	ta	CHISQDIST(Number; Degrees Of Freedom; Cumulative)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090239564				0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the function is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395660				0	ta	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395623				0	ta	            \<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional): 0 or False calculates the probability density function. Other values or True or omitted calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150603				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603				0	ta	EXPONDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXPONVERT\"\>Returns the exponential distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153789				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150987				0	ta	EXPONDIST(Number; Lambda; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	119			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569	120			0	ta	            \<emph\>Lambda\</emph\> is the parameter value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147332	121			0	ta	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> is a logical value that determines the form of the function. \<emph\>C = 0\</emph\> calculates the density function, and \<emph\>C = 1\</emph\> calculates the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146133				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150357	123			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EXPONDIST(3;0.5;1)\</item\> returns 0.78.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	AutoInput				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	bm_id2486037				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>entering entries with AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148492				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"AutoInput\"\>AutoInput\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoComplete\"\>Switches the AutoInput function on and off, which automatically completes entries, based on other entries in the same column.\</ahelp\> The column is scanned up to a maximum of 2000 cells or 200 different strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ta	The completion text is highlighted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	ta	To accept the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or a cursor key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	ta	To append text or to edit the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	ta	To view more completions, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to scroll forward, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to scroll backward.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	ta	To see a list of all available AutoInput text items for the current column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	ta	When typing formulas using characters that match previous entries, a Help tip will appear listing the last ten functions used from \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, from all defined range names, from all database range names, and from the content of all label ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	ta	AutoInput is case-sensitive. If, for example, you have written "Total" in a cell, you cannot enter "total" in another cell of the same column without first deactivating AutoInput.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Array Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147273				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>array formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inline array constants\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions;array functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; array formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; array formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting array ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;conditional calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>matrices; calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional calculations with arrays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>implicit array handling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forced array handling\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147273				0	ta	Array Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154744				0	ta	\<variable id=\"matrixtext\"\>This category contains the array functions. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146084				0	ta	What is an Array?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154298				0	ta	\<variable id=\"wasmatrix\"\>An array is a linked range of cells on a spreadsheet containing values. \</variable\> A square range of 3 rows and 3 columns is a 3 x 3 array:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154692				0	ta	A				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150117				0	ta	B				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325				0	ta	C				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	ta	1				20200411 15:09:53
