helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621				0	ta	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	ta	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903491982				0	ta	If the text string also includes a time value, DATEVALUE only returns the integer part of the conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268				0	ta	DATEVALUE("Text")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	ta	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	ta	         \<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	ta	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ta	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ta	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	ta	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	ta	Select the cells that will be unprotected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	ta	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	ta	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	ta	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	ta	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	ta	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	ta	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	ta	Password (optional)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	ta	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Mark Invalid Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153821				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>cells; invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; showing invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invalid data;marking\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>Mark Invalid Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowInvalid\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Marks all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	ta	The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"validity rules\"\>validity rules\</link\> restrict the input of numbers, dates, time values and text to certain values. However, it is possible to enter invalid values or copy invalid values into the cells if the \<emph\>Stop\</emph\> option is not selected. When you assign a validity rule, existing values in a cell will not be modified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	EASTERSUNDAY				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152960				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>EASTERSUNDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152960				0	ta	\<variable id=\"eastersunday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_eastersunday.xhp\"\>EASTERSUNDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OSTERSONNTAG\"\>Returns the date of Easter Sunday for the entered year.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id9460127				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id2113711				0	ta	EASTERSUNDAY(Year)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3938413				0	ta	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9956 or 0 and 99. You can also calculate other holidays by simple addition with this date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	ta	Easter Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147521				0	ta	Good Friday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) - 2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146072				0	ta	Pentecost Sunday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 49				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149553				0	ta	Pentecost Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 50				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155120				0	ta	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	ta	=EASTERSUNDAY(2000) returns 2000-04-23.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	ta	EASTERSUNDAY(2000)+49 returns the internal serial number 36688. The result is 2000-06-11. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Error Alert				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120300.xhp\" name=\"Error Alert\"\>Error Alert\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TABPAGE:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR\"\>Define the error message that is displayed when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ta	You can also start a macro with an error message. A sample macro is provided at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	ta	Show error message when invalid values are entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the error message that you enter in the \<emph\>Contents\</emph\> area when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> If enabled, the message is displayed to prevent an invalid entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984	5			0	ta	In both cases, if you select "Stop", the invalid entry is deleted and the previous value is reentered in the cell. The same applies if you close the "Warning" and "Information" dialogs by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel \</emph\>button. If you close the dialogs with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button, the invalid entry is not deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152460				0	ta	Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	ta	Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:LB_ACTION\"\>Select the action that you want to occur when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> The "Stop" action rejects the invalid entry and displays a dialog that you have to close by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The "Warning" and "Information" actions display a dialog that can be closed by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> or \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>. The invalid entry is only rejected when you click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	ta	Browse				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153160				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:BTN_SEARCH\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\> dialog where you can select the macro that is executed when invalid data is entered in a cell. The macro is executed after the error message is displayed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153876				0	ta	Title				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149410				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:EDT_TITLE\"\>Enter the title of the macro or the error message that you want to display when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154510				0	ta	Error message				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149122				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MULTILINEEDIT:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:EDT_ERROR\"\>Enter the message that you want to display when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	ta	\<emph\>Sample macro:\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Statistical Functions Part Five				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147072				0	ta	\<variable id=\"rz\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060185.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Five\"\>Statistical Functions Part Five\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155071				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>RANK function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>numbers;determining ranks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155071				0	ta	RANK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153976				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RANG\"\>Returns the rank of a number in a sample.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159206				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153250				0	ta	RANK(Value; Data; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154543	6			0	ta	            \<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the value, whose rank is to be determined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149130	7			0	ta	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215	8			0	ta	            \<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the sequence order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id9305398				0	ta	Type = 0 means descending from the last item of the array to the first (this is the default), 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id9996948				0	ta	Type = 1 means ascending from the first item of the range to the last.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143223				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919	10			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=RANK(A10;A1:A50)\</item\> returns the ranking of the value in A10 in value range A1:A50. If \<item type=\"literal\"\>Value\</item\> does not exist within the range an error message is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153556				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>SKEW function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153556				0	ta	SKEW				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153485				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SCHIEFE\"\>Returns the skewness of a distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154733				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	ta	SKEW(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155757	16			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number1, Number2...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153297				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118	18			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SKEW(A1:A50)\</item\> calculates the value of skew for the data referenced.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149051				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>regression lines;FORECAST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>extrapolations\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>FORECAST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149051				0	ta	FORECAST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153290				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SCHAETZER\"\>Extrapolates future values based on existing x and y values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151343				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	ta	FORECAST(Value; DataY; DataX)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148743	24			0	ta	            \<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the x value, for which the y value on the linear regression is to be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325	25			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataY\</emph\> is the array or range of known y's.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536	26			0	ta	            \<emph\>DataX\</emph\> is the array or range of known x's.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147416				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874	28			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FORECAST(50;A1:A50;B1;B50)\</item\> returns the Y value expected for the X value of 50 if the X and Y values in both references are linked by a linear trend.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149143				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>STDEV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>standard deviations in statistics;based on a sample\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149143				0	ta	STDEV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_STABW\"\>Estimates the standard deviation based on a sample.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146815				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	33			0	ta	STDEV(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3157904	34			0	ta	            \<emph\>Number1, Number2, ... Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges representing a sample based on an entire population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150650				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149434	36			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=STDEV(A1:A50)\</item\> returns the estimated standard deviation based on the data referenced.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144745				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>STDEVA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144745				0	ta	STDEVA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_STABWA\"\>Calculates the standard deviation of an estimation based on a sample.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148884				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	ta	STDEVA(Value1;Value2;...Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154547	190			0	ta	            \<emph\>Value1, Value2, ...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges representing a sample derived from an entire population. Text has the value 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155829				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581	192			0	ta	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=STDEVA(A1:A50)\</item\> returns the estimated standard deviation based on the data referenced.				20200411 15:09:53
