helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153328				0	ta	\<emph\>Yield\</emph\> is the annual yield of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149186				0	ta	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149726				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153111				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	ta	Settlement date: February 7 1999, maturity date: June 15 1999, last interest: October 15 1998. Interest rate: 3.75 per cent, yield: 4.05 per cent, redemption value: 100 currency units, frequency of payments: half-yearly = 2, basis: = 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148567				0	ta	The price per 100 currency units per value of a security, which has an irregular last interest date, is calculated as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150332				0	ta	=ODDLPRICE("1999-02-07";"1999-06-15";"1998-10-15"; 0.0375; 0.0405;100;2;0) returns 99.87829.				20200411 15:09:53
