helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150572				0	ta	=ODDLYIELD("1999-04-20";"1999-06-15"; "1998-10-15"; 0.0375; 99.875; 100;2;0) returns 0.044873 or 4.4873%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variable declining depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>depreciations;variable declining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>VDB function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	ta	VDB				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VDB\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified or partial period using a variable declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155519				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025				0	ta	VDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; S; End; Factor; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150692				0	ta	\<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial value of an asset.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155369				0	ta	\<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154954				0	ta	\<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the depreciation duration of the asset.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152817				0	ta	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the start of the depreciation. A must be entered in the same date unit as the duration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	ta	\<emph\>End\</emph\> is the end of the depreciation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147536				0	ta	\<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the depreciation factor. Factor = 2 is double rate depreciation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	232			0	ta	\<emph\>Type \</emph\>is an optional parameter. Type = 1 means a switch to linear depreciation. In Type = 0 no switch is made.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0D				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148429				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927				0	ta	What is the declining-balance double-rate depreciation for a period if the initial cost is 35,000 currency units and the value at the end of the depreciation is 7,500 currency units. The depreciation period is 3 years. The depreciation from the 10th to the 20th period is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=VDB(35000;7500;36;10;20;2)\</item\> = 8603.80 currency units. The depreciation during the period between the 10th and the 20th period is 8,603.80 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147485				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XIRR function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147485				0	ta	XIRR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XIRR\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E62				0	ta	If the payments take place at regular intervals, use the IRR function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146149				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149826				0	ta	XIRR(Values; Dates; Guess)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163821				0	ta	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> and \<emph\>Dates\</emph\> refer to a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149708				0	ta	\<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) is a guess that can be input for the internal rate of return. The default is 10%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145085				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149273				0	ta	Calculation of the internal rate of return for the following five payments:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155838				0	ta	A				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152934				0	ta	B				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	ta	C				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147083				0	ta	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	ta	2001-01-01				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145212				0	ta	-\<item type=\"input\"\>10000\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>Received\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153277				0	ta	2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154052				0	ta	2001-01-02				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151297				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149985				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>Deposited\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154744				0	ta	3				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151				0	ta	2001-03-15				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145657				0	ta	2500				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155101				0	ta	4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146894				0	ta	2001-05-12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3143231				0	ta	5000				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156012				0	ta	5				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149758				0	ta	2001-08-10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	ta	1000				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152793				0	ta	=XIRR(B1:B5; A1:A5; 0.1) returns 0.1828.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149198				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>XNPV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149198				0	ta	XNPV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153904				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XNPV\"\>Calculates the capital value (net present value)for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN11138				0	ta	If the payments take place at regular intervals, use the NPV function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155323				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150117				0	ta	XNPV(Rate; Values; Dates)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153100				0	ta	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the internal rate of return for the payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155395				0	ta	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> and \<emph\>Dates\</emph\> refer to a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148832				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150525				0	ta	Calculation of the net present value for the above-mentioned five payments for a notional internal rate of return of 6%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149910				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XNPV(0.06;B1:B5;A1:A5)\</item\> returns 323.02.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148822				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rates of return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RRI function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148822				0	ta	RRI				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154293				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZGZ\"\>Calculates the interest rate resulting from the profit (return) of an investment.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148444				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148804				0	ta	RRI(P; PV; FV)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154901				0	ta	\<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of periods needed for calculating the interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	ta	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771				0	ta	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> determines what is desired as the cash value of the deposit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148941				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	ta	For four periods (years) and a cash value of 7,500 currency units, the interest rate of the return is to be calculated if the future value is 10,000 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775	246			0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RRI(4;7500;10000)\</item\> = 7.46 %				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145413	247			0	ta	The interest rate must be 7.46 % so that 7,500 currency units will become 10,000 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154267				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154267				0	ta	RATE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINS\"\>Returns the constant interest rate per period of an annuity.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158423				0	ta	RATE(NPer; Pmt; PV; FV; Type; Guess)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148910				0	ta	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which payments are made (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	ta	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant payment (annuity) paid during each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149160				0	ta	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the cash value in the sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456				0	ta	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153243				0	ta	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the periodic payment, either at the beginning or at the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	ta	\<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) determines the estimated value of the interest with iterative calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E2A				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149791				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	ta	What is the constant interest rate for a payment period of 3 periods if 10 currency units are paid regularly and the present cash value is 900 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RATE(3;10;900)\</item\> = -121% The interest rate is therefore 121%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149106				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>INTRATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149106				0	ta	INTRATE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_INTRATE\"\>Calculates the annual interest rate that results when a security (or other item) is purchased at an investment value and sold at a redemption value. No interest is paid.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149974				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149800				0	ta	INTRATE(Settlement; Maturity; Investment; Redemption; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148988				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security is sold.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154604				0	ta	\<emph\>Investment\</emph\> is the purchase price.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154337				0	ta	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the selling price.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145380				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149426				0	ta	A painting is bought on 1990-01-15 for 1 million and sold on 2002-05-05 for 2 million. The basis is daily balance calculation (basis = 3). What is the average annual level of interest?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151125				0	ta	=INTRATE("1990-01-15"; "2002-05-05"; 1000000; 2000000; 3) returns 8.12%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148654				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPNCD function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148654				0	ta	COUPNCD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149927				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPNCD\"\>Returns the date of the first interest date after the settlement date. Format the result as a date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153317				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150423				0	ta	COUPNCD(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150628				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155424				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154794				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) when is the next interest date?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159251				0	ta	=COUPNCD("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2001-05-15.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143281				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143281				0	ta	COUPDAYS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYS\"\>Returns the number of days in the current interest period in which the settlement date falls.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148685				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	ta	COUPDAYS(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152767				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146126				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153705				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days are there in the interest period in which the settlement date falls?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338				0	ta	=COUPDAYS("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 181.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154832				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYSNC function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154832				0	ta	COUPDAYSNC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYSNC\"\>Returns the number of days from the settlement date until the next interest date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155121				0	ta	COUPDAYSNC(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158440				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146075				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154620	159			0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency \</emph\>is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155604				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148671				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days are there until the next interest payment?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156158				0	ta	=COUPDAYSNC("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 110.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150408				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPDAYBS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>durations;first interest payment until settlement date\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>securities;first interest payment until settlement date\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150408				0	ta	COUPDAYBS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPDAYBS\"\>Returns the number of days from the first day of interest payment on a security until the settlement date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156142				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159083				0	ta	COUPDAYBS(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146907				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154414				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days is this?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151103				0	ta	=COUPDAYBS("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 71.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152957				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPPCD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates;interest date prior to settlement date\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152957				0	ta	COUPPCD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPPCD\"\>Returns the date of the interest date prior to the settlement date. Format the result as a date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156269				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790				0	ta	COUPPCD(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150989				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154667				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148968				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) what was the interest date prior to purchase?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	ta	=COUPPCD("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2000-15-11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150673				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>COUPNUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of coupons\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150673				0	ta	COUPNUM				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154350				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPNUM\"\>Returns the number of coupons (interest payments) between the settlement date and the maturity date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148400				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153200				0	ta	COUPNUM(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159406				0	ta	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	ta	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154720				0	ta	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149319				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	ta	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many interest dates are there?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	ta	=COUPNUM("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149339				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>IPMT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>periodic amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149339				0	ta	IPMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154522				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINSZ\"\>Calculates the periodic amortizement for an investment with regular payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153266				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151283				0	ta	IPMT(Rate; Period; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147313				0	ta	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145158				0	ta	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the period, for which the compound interest is calculated. Period=NPER if compound interest for the last period is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147577				0	ta	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156211				0	ta	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213				0	ta	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) at the end of the periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154195				0	ta	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date for the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150102				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	ta	What is the interest rate during the fifth period (year) if the constant interest rate is 5% and the cash value is 15,000 currency units? The periodic payment is seven years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150496				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=IPMT(5%;5;7;15000)\</item\> = -352.97 currency units. The compound interest during the fifth period (year) is 352.97 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151205				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;future values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151205				0	ta	FV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZW\"\>Returns the future value of an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate (Future Value).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145215				0	ta	FV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; PV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ta	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	ta	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	ta	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the annuity paid regularly per period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	ta	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> (optional) is the (present) cash value of an investment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150999				0	ta	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines whether the payment is due at the beginning or the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN114D8				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146800				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146813				0	ta	What is the value at the end of an investment if the interest rate is 4% and the payment period is two years, with a periodic payment of 750 currency units. The investment has a present value of 2,500 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FV(4%;2;750;2500) \</item\>= -4234.00 currency units. The value at the end of the investment is 4234.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155912				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>FVSCHEDULE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;varying interest rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155912				0	ta	FVSCHEDULE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163726				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FVSCHEDULE\"\>Calculates the accumulated value of the starting capital for a series of periodically varying interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149571				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148891				0	ta	FVSCHEDULE(Principal; Schedule)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148904				0	ta	\<emph\>Principal\</emph\> is the starting capital.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148562				0	ta	\<emph\>Schedule\</emph\> is a series of interest rates, for example, as a range H3:H5 or as a (List) (see example).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147288				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148638				0	ta	1000 currency units have been invested in for three years. The interest rates were 3%, 4% and 5% per annum. What is the value after three years?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156358				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FVSCHEDULE(1000;{0.03;0.04;0.05})\</item\> returns 1124.76.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156435				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>payment periods;number of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NPER function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156435				0	ta	NPER				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZZR\"\>Returns the number of periods for an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147216				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	ta	NPER(Rate; Pmt; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	ta	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149042				0	ta	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant annuity paid in each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	ta	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	ta	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the last period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145127				0	ta	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the payment at the beginning or at the end of the period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN1166C				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155795				0	ta	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147378				0	ta	How many payment periods does a payment period cover with a periodic interest rate of 6%, a periodic payment of 153.75 currency units and a present cash value of 2.600 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156171				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NPER(6%;153.75;2600)\</item\> = -12,02. The payment period covers 12.02 periods.				20200411 15:09:53
