helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	ta	Case sensitive				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	ta	Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156327				0	ta	Regular Expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	ta	Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	ta	If the \<emph\>Regular Expression\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use EQUAL (=) and NOT EQUAL (<>) also in comparisons. You can also use the following functions: DCOUNTA, DGET, MATCH, COUNTIF, SUMIF, LOOKUP, VLOOKUP and HLOOKUP.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	ta	Unique records only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ta	Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.				20200411 15:09:53
