helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ViewValueHighlighting\"\>Displays cell contents in different colors, depending on type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ta	To remove the highlighting, unmark the menu entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	ta	Text cells are formatted in black, formulas in green, and number cells in blue, no matter how their display is formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	ta	If this function is active, colors that you define in the document will not be displayed. When you deactivate the function, the user-defined colors are displayed again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Text to Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	bm_id8004394				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>text to columns\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	hd_id2300180				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/text2columns.xhp\"\>Text to Columns\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id655232				0	ta	\<variable id=\"text2columns\"\>Opens the Text to Columns dialog, where you enter settings to expand the contents of selected cells to multiple cells. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	hd_id9599597				0	ta	To expand cell contents to multiple cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id2021546				0	ta	You can expand cells that contain comma separated values (CSV) into multiple cells in the same row. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id2623981				0	ta	For example, cell A1 contains the comma separated values \<item type=\"literal\"\>1,2,3,4\</item\>, and cell A2 contains the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>A,B,C,D\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id7242042				0	ta	Select the cell or cells that you want to expand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id6999420				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Data - Text to Columns\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id6334116				0	ta	You see the Text to Columns dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id9276406				0	ta	Select the separator options. The preview shows how the current cell contents will be transformed into multiple cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id8523819				0	ta	You can select a fixed width and then click the ruler on the preview to set cell breakup positions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id1517380				0	ta	You can select or enter separator characters to define the positions of breaking points. The separator characters are removed from the resulting cell contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id7110812				0	ta	In the example, you select the comma as a delimiter character. Cells A1 and A2 will be expanded to four columns each. A1 contains 1, B1 contains 2, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Column Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151384				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;deleting column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;manual column breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column breaks;deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02190200.xhp\" name=\"Column Break\"\>Column Break\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteColumnbreak\"\>Removes a manual column break to the left of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	ta	Position the cursor in the cell to the right of the column break indicated by a vertical line and choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Column Break\</emph\>. The manual column break is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Row Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156326				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; deleting row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;manual row breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>row breaks; deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156326				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02190100.xhp\" name=\"Row Break\"\>Row Break\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteRowbreak\"\>Removes the manual row break above the active cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ta	Position the cursor in a cell directly below the row break indicated by a horizontal line and choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Row Break\</emph\>. The manual row break is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Criteria				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	bm_id1464278				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>selection lists;validity\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153032				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120100.xhp\" name=\"Criteria\"\>Criteria\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156327				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TABPAGE:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES\"\>Specify the validation rules for the selected cell(s).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	ta	For example, you can define criteria such as: "Numbers between 1 and 10" or "Texts that are no more than 20 characters".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ta	Allow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:LB_ALLOW\"\>Click a validation option for the selected cell(s).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ta	The following conditions are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	ta	Condition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ta	Effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	ta	All values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	ta	No limitation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	ta	Whole number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ta	Only whole numbers corresponding to the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802				0	ta	Decimal				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153160				0	ta	All numbers corresponding to the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ta	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150718				0	ta	All numbers corresponding to the condition. The entered values are formatted accordingly the next time the dialog is called up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	ta	Time				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	ta	All numbers corresponding to the condition. The entered values are formatted accordingly the next time the dialog is called up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	ta	Cell range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	ta	Allow only values that are given in a cell range. The cell range can be specified explicitly, or as a named database range, or as a named range. The range may consist of one column or one row of cells. If you specify a range of columns and rows, only the first column is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	ta	List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	ta	Allow only values or strings specified in a list. Strings and values can be mixed. Numbers evaluate to their value, so if you enter the number 1 in the list, the entry 100% is also valid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	ta	Text length				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	ta	Entries whose length corresponds to the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	ta	Allow empty cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153967				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TRISTATEBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:TSB_ALLOW_BLANKS\"\>In conjunction with \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Mark invalid Data\</emph\>, this defines that empty cells are shown as invalid data (disabled) or not (enabled).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10709				0	ta	Show selection list				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SHOWLIST\"\>Shows a list of all valid strings or values to select from. The list can also be opened by selecting the cell and pressing Ctrl+D (Mac: Command+D).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10724				0	ta	Sort entries ascending				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:CB_SORTLIST\"\>Sorts the selection list in ascending order and filters duplicates from the list. If not checked, the order from the data source is taken.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073F				0	ta	Source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:Edit:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_MIN\"\>Enter the cell range that contains the valid values or text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	ta	Entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:MultiLineEdit:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_LIST\"\>Enter the entries that will be valid values or text strings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163807				0	ta	Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144502	10			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:LB_VALUE\"\>Select the comparative operator that you want to use.\</ahelp\> The available operators depend on what you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box. If you select "between" or "not between", the \<emph\>Minimum\</emph\> and \<emph\>Maximum\</emph\> input boxes appear. Otherwise, only the \<emph\>Minimum\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Maximum, or the Value\</emph\> input boxes appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153782				0	ta	Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153266	12			0	ta	Enter the value for the data validation option that you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149814				0	ta	Minimum				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153199	14			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_MIN\"\>Enter the minimum value for the data validation option that you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149035				0	ta	Maximum				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	16			0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:TP_VALIDATION_VALUES:EDT_MAX\"\>Enter the maximum value for the data validation option that you selected in the \<emph\>Allow \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Edit Print Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	ta	Edit Print Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159488				0	ta	\<variable id=\"druckbereichetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditPrintArea\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify the print range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also set the rows or columns which are to be repeated in every page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AE				0	ta	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp#printranges\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	ta	Print range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_PRINTAREA\"\>Allows you to modify a defined print range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	ta	Select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a print range definition for the current spreadsheet. Select \<emph\>-entire sheet-\</emph\> to set the current sheet as a print range. Select \<emph\>-selection-\</emph\> to define the selected area of a spreadsheet as the print range. By selecting \<emph\>-user-defined-\</emph\>, you can define a print range that you have already defined using the \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\> command. If you have given a name to a range using the \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\> command, this name will be displayed and can be selected from the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ta	In the right-hand text box, you can enter a print range by reference or by name. If the cursor is in the \<emph\>Print range\</emph\> text box, you can also select the print range in the spreadsheet with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	ta	Rows to repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATROW\"\>Choose one or more rows to print on every page. In the right text box enter the row reference, for example, "1" or "$1" or "$2:$3".\</ahelp\> The list box displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	ta	You can also define repeating rows by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149581				0	ta	Columns to repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATCOL\"\>Choose one or more columns to print on every page. In the right text box enter the column reference, for example, "A" or "AB" or "$C:$E".\</ahelp\> The list box then displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ta	You can also define repeating columns by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	SECOND 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159390				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>SECOND function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159390				0	ta	\<variable id=\"second\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_second.xhp\"\>SECOND\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148974				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SEKUNDE\"\>Returns the second for the given time value.\</ahelp\> The second is given as an integer between 0 and 59.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362				0	ta	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407				0	ta	SECOND(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	ta	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the second is to be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992				0	ta	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3153350				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(NOW())\</item\> returns the current second				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3150831				0	ta	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(C4)\</item\> returns 17 if contents of C4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>12:20:17\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Protecting document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	ta	Protecting document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	ta	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	ta	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	ta	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ta	Password (optional)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	ta	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	ta	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				20200411 15:09:53
