helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	ta	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	ta	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	ta	To apply a gradient:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ta	Select a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	ta	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	ta	Creating Custom Gradients				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	ta	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20200411 15:09:53
