helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	ta	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	ta	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Drawing Sectors and Segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	ta	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	ta	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	ta	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	ta	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	ta	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ta	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	ta	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ta	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	ta	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	ta	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	ta	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	ta	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	ta	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ta	Arranging Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	ta	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	ta	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	ta	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	ta	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	ta	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	ta	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	ta	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	ta	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	ta	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ta	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	ta	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	ta	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	ta	Aligning Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	ta	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	ta	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	ta	Distributing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ta	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	ta	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	ta	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ta	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Grouping Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	ta	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	ta	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	ta	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ta	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ta	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	ta	To group objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	ta	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ta	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	ta	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	ta	Selecting Objects in a Group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	ta	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ta	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20200411 15:09:53
