helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ta	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	ta	Regular Expression Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	ta	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	ta	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	ta	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	ta	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	ta	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	ta	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Using Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>multi-column text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; multi-column\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in/use of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	ta	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	ta	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	ta	To prevent text from being edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	ta	To show or hide text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	ta	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ta	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	ta	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ta	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	ta	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	ta	Sections and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ta	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	ta	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets/numbers; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	ta	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525				0	ta	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	ta	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	ta	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	ta	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	ta	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	ta	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	ta	Press Enter again to finish the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	ta	You can start a numbered list with any number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Creating Non-printing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>non-printing text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; non-printable\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856				0	ta	\<variable id=\"nonprintable_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/nonprintable_text.xhp\" name=\"Creating Non-printing Text\"\>Creating Non-printing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id4685201				0	ta	To create text that is not to be printed do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149789				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\> and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	ta	Enter text in the frame and if you want, resize the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150242				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame/Object\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145227				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150320				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\nonprintable_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3138828				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145083				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;objects from Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145083				0	ta	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\"\>Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	ta	You can drag-and-drop an object from the gallery into a text document, spreadsheet, drawing, or presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	ta	To replace a gallery object that you inserted in a document, hold down Shift+Ctrl, and then drag a different gallery object onto the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; styles, by fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	ta	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ta	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	ta	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	ta	Click the style, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fill Format Mode\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	ta	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	ta	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	ta	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	ta	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	ta	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	ta	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	ta	Open a new text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	ta	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	ta	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Left Page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	ta	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Right Page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	ta	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	ta	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Adding Input Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155916				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>text; input fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields; input fields in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input fields in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;input fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916	1			0	ta	\<variable id=\"fields_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Input Fields\"\>Adding Input Fields\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	ta	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialog where you can edit the variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	ta	Click “Input field” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and type the text for the variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708				0	ta	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	ta	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	ta	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	ta	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	ta	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	ta	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	ta	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	ta	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	ta	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	ta	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	ta	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	ta	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ta	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	ta	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	ta	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	ta	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	ta	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	ta	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ta	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	ta	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\> box, select the paragraph style that you want to use to generate a new HTML page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	ta	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
