helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting Cross-References				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	ta	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	ta	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	ta	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	ta	Cross-Referencing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	ta	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	ta	To Insert a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	ta	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list, select “Set Reference”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	ta	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>. The name of the target is added to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	ta	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	ta	To Create a Cross-Reference to a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7032074				0	ta	Position the cursor in the text where you want to insert a cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7796868				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\> to open the dialog, if it is not open already.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	ta	Cross-Referencing an Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	ta	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	ta	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	ta	Updating Cross-References				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	ta	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7321390				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\> to switch between viewing the reference names and the reference contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Moving and Copying Text in Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>sections;moving and copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;cut/copied text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mouse;moving and copying text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	ta	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	ta	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	ta	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154236				0	ta	To move the selected text, drag the text to a different location in the document and release. While you drag, the mouse pointer changes to include a gray box.\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3153148\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153148\"\>Mouse cursor moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257	14			0	ta	To copy the selected text, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to include a plus sign (+).\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3152868\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152868\"\>Mouse cursor copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Hiding Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables;for hiding text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	ta	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	ta	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	ta	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	ta	To Create a Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	ta	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	ta	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	ta	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	ta	Enter a value for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	ta	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	ta	To Hide Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	ta	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	ta	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	ta	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	ta	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	ta	To Hide a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	ta	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	ta	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	ta	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	ta	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675				0	ta	To Hide a Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	ta	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\>, and then enter an expression in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	ta	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3846858				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text_display.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Hidden Text\"\>Displaying Hidden Text\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id8148442				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/nonprintable_text.xhp\" name=\"Creating Non-printing Text\"\>Creating Non-printing Text\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148603				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Fields - Other\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147011				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>Insert - Section\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147029				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of Operators\"\>List of Operators\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Going to Specific Bookmark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145778				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; positioning cursor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>jumping;to bookmarks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	ta	\<variable id=\"jump2statusbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/jump2statusbar.xhp\" name=\"Going to Specific Bookmark\"\>Going to Specific Bookmark\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178	31			0	ta	To go to a specific bookmark in your document, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>hold down Ctrl and click \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>right-click\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> field on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>, and then choose the bookmark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Bookmark\"\>Insert Bookmark\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	ta	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	ta	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with fixed row and column dimensions if space permits.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	ta	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	ta	To set the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options for tables in text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, or use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed\</item\>, \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed/Proportional\</item\>, and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variable\</item\> icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar. There are three display modes for tables:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	ta	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	ta	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	ta	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Using AutoText				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155521				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>AutoText\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>networks and AutoText directories\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blocks of text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	ta	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	ta	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	ta	To To Create an AutoText Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	ta	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - AutoText\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	ta	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	ta	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	ta	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	ta	To Insert an AutoText Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	ta	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	ta	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644				0	ta	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	ta	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoText\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	ta	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>fn\</item\>, and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>dt\</item\>, and then press F3. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	ta	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	ta	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	ta	Using AutoText in Network Installations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	ta	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	ta	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ta	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	ta	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154995				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>Edit - AutoText\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
