helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	ta	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	ta	In the document, click from where you want to copy the updated style. For example, click a paragraph to which you applied some manual formatting that you want to copy now.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	ta	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the style that you want to update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	ta	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and choose \<emph\>Update Style\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id0310200910360780				0	ta	Only the manually formatted attributes of the text at the cursor position in the document will be added to the style that is selected in the Styles and Formatting window. Any attributes that were applied as part of a style will not be added to the updated style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
