helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	bm_id6737876				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>borders;for text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;borders in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders in Writer\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;around text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3614917				0	ta	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	ta	You can apply a variety of different cell borders to selected cells in a Writer table and to the whole table. Other objects in text documents can have user defined borders, too. For example, you can assign borders to page styles, to frames, and to inserted pictures or charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	ta	Select the cell or a block of cells in a Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6129947				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table properties\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	ta	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6016418				0	ta	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5282448				0	ta	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
