helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	ta	Click in the document where you want to insert the index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	ta	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Index/Table\</item\> tab, select the name of the user-defined index that you created in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146881				0	ta	Select any options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150720				0	ta	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\>, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the box. Click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
