helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	ta	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	ta	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147684				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>captions; adding chapter numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering;of objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	ta	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	ta	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	ta	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	ta	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	19			0	ta	Select a caption title from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, and select a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> box. \<br/\>You also can enter a caption text in this dialog. If you want, enter text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Caption\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	ta	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> box, select the number of heading levels to include in the chapter number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	ta	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ta	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	ta	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
