helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149686				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>words; counting in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; counting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>counting words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word counts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	ta	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	ta	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Word Count\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id1116200901133957				0	ta	How does %PRODUCTNAME count words?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133998				0	ta	In general, every string of characters between two spaces is a word. Tabs, line breaks, and paragraph breaks are word limits, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133985				0	ta	Words with dashes or always visible hyphens, as in plug-in, add-on, user/config, are counted as one word each.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id111620090113399				0	ta	The words can be a mix of letters, numbers, and special characters. So the following text counts as four words: abc123 1.23 "$" http://www.example.com.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	ta	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Removing Line Breaks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;removing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	ta	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ta	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	ta	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	ta	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Word Completion for Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;using/disabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	ta	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	ta	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	ta	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	ta	 To Accept/Reject a Word Completion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	ta	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	ta	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	ta	 To Switch off the Word Completion 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	ta	 Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	ta	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id7504806				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Applying Text Formatting While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149689				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>text; formatting bold while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; bold, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;bold formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bold;formatting while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;bold formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	ta	\<variable id=\"shortcut_writing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/shortcut_writing.xhp\" name=\"Applying Text Formatting While You Type\"\>Applying Text Formatting While You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155909				0	ta	To apply bold formatting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ta	Select the text that you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836	5			0	ta	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156112	6			0	ta	You can also press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B, type the text that you want to format in bold, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B when you are finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard shortcut for text documents\"\>Keyboard shortcut for text documents\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
