helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	ta	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	ta	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	ta	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	ta	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	ta	To define a caption proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	ta	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	ta	Select the options that you want, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Figure\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ta	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	ta	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption category. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	ta	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	ta	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the Sum of a Series of Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	ta	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	ta	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sum\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table Bar\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\> appears with the entry "=sum".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	ta	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	ta	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	ta	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	ta	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting a Graphic From a File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting by dialog\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures, by dialog\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	ta	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Graphic From a File\"\>Inserting a Graphic From a File\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914				0	ta	Click in the document where you want to insert the graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	ta	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - From File\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156021				0	ta	Locate the graphic file that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ta	By default, the inserted graphic is centered above the paragraph that you clicked in.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>tables;start/end of document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;inserting before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;paragraphs before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	ta	\<variable id=\"insert_beforetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_beforetable.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\"\>Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	ta	If you want to insert text before a table that is at the top of a page, click in the first cell of the table, in front of any contents of that cell, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_idN10612				0	ta	To insert text after a table at the end of the document, go to the last cell of the table and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;text objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	ta	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7355265				0	ta	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for various objects in $[officename] Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	ta	To Apply a Background To Text Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ta	Select the characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ta	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	ta	To Apply a Background To a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	ta	Place the cursor in the paragraph or select several paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id0104201010554939				0	ta	To select an object in the background, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key and click the object. Alternatively, use the Navigator to select the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	ta	To Apply a Background To All or Part of a Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	ta	Place the cursor in the table in your text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ta	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	ta	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ta	In the \<emph\>For\</emph\> box, choose whether the color or graphic should apply to the current cell, the current row or the whole table. If you select several cells or rows before opening the dialog, the change applies to the selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151041				0	ta	You may also use an icon to apply a background to table parts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ta	To apply a background color to cells, select the cells and click the color on the \<emph\>Background Color\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	ta	To apply a background color to a text paragraph within a cell, place the cursor into the text paragraph, then click the color on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Background Color\</item\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\"\>Highlighting icon\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>Background tab page\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id4922025				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id478530				0	ta	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Page Backgrounds as Page Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
