helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154248				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; across multiple text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating across\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	ta	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	ta	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	ta	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	ta	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	ta	Press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ta	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	ta	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Numbering and Numbering Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; manually/by styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>manual numbering in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles;numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174	30			0	ta	\<variable id=\"using_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Numbering and Numbering Styles\"\>Numbering and Numbering Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149818				0	ta	You can apply numbering to a paragraph manually or with a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id6140629				0	ta	To Apply Numbering Manually				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	ta	To apply numbering manually, click in the paragraph, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153405				0	ta	You cannot apply manual numbering to paragraphs that are listed under "Special Styles" in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10711				0	ta	When you press Enter in a numbered or bulleted list, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically numbers the next paragraph. To remove the numbering or bullet from the new paragraph, press Enter again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	ta	To change the hierarchical level of a bullet in a list, click in front of the paragraph, then press the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072F				0	ta	To change the bullets or numbering format for the current paragraph only, select a character or word in the paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10733				0	ta	To change the bullet or numbering format for all paragraphs in the list, ensure that the cursor is in the list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a new format. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	ta	To apply the same bullet or numbering format to all paragraphs in the list, select all paragraphs, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>, and then click a format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073A				0	ta	You can also use the commands on the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Object Bar\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> toolbar to edit a numbered or bulleted list. To change the numbering or bullet format, click the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153123				0	ta	To Apply Numbering With a Paragraph Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153137				0	ta	Paragraph Styles give you greater control over numbering that you apply in a document. When you change the numbering format of the style, all paragraphs using the style are automatically updated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	ta	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Styles\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	ta	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to apply numbering to, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149850				0	ta	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Outline & Numbering\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	ta	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering Style\</item\> box, select the type of numbering that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	ta	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	ta	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to add numbering to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ta	Calculating in Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	ta	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;in Writer tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	ta	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	ta	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	ta	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	ta	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=10000/12\</item\>, and then press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	ta	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	ta	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
