helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150493				0	ta	Edit Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	ta	\<variable id=\"feldbefehltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FieldDialog\"\>Opens a dialog where you can edit the properties of a field. Click in front of a field, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\> In the dialog, you can use the arrow buttons to move to the previous or the next field.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	ta	You can also double-click a field in your document to open the field for editing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	ta	To change the view between field names and field contents in your document, choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106	59			0	ta	If you select a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link in your document, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields, \</emph\>the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02180000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Links\"\>\<emph\>Edit Links\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	ta	If you click in front of a "sender" type field, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>, the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010100.xhp\" name=\"User data\"\>\<emph\>User data\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145765				0	ta	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	ta	Lists the type of field that you are editing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151371				0	ta	The following dialog elements are only visible when the corresponding field type is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150687				0	ta	Select				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	ta	Lists the field options, for example, "fixed". If you want, you can click another option for the selected field type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155854				0	ta	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	ta	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKNUMFORMAT\"\>Select the format for the contents of the field. For date, time, and user-defined fields, you can also click "Additional formats" in the list, and then choose a different format.\</ahelp\> The formats that are available depend on the type of field that you are editing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149556				0	ta	Offset				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	ta	Displays the offset for the selected field type, for example, for "Next Page," "Page Numbers" or "Previous Page". You can enter a new offset value which will be added to the displayed page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	ta	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145269				0	ta	Level				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150559				0	ta	Change the defined values and outline levels for the "Chapter" field type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147744				0	ta	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149834				0	ta	Displays the name of a field variable. If you want, you can enter a new name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148844				0	ta	Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148857				0	ta	Displays the current value of the field variable. If you want, you can enter a new value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153306				0	ta	Condition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156124				0	ta	Displays the condition that must be met for the field to be activated. If you want, you can enter a new \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156103				0	ta	Then, Else				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155073				0	ta	Change the field contents that are displayed depending on whether the field condition is met or not.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154326				0	ta	Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154339				0	ta	Insert or modify the reference text for the selected field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148785				0	ta	Macro name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	ta	Displays the name of the macro assigned to the selected field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150097				0	ta	Placeholder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150027				0	ta	Displays the placeholder text of the selected field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150041				0	ta	Insert Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	ta	Displays the text that is linked to a condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140				0	ta	Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154624				0	ta	Displays the formula of a formula field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150658				0	ta	Database selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150671				0	ta	Select a registered database that you want to insert the selected field from. You can also change the table or query that the selected field refers to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154025				0	ta	Record number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154039	39			0	ta	Displays the database record number that is inserted when the condition specified for the "Any record" field type is met. 				20200411 15:09:53
